+Thank you for sending the log! It showed exactly where Neutrino stops, and it led us to a second problem.
+
+**What was wrong:** the UDPFS network driver had a bug. When a file read from your PC had an odd size, its last byte arrived wrong. Your `neutrino` folder on mc1 has 29 files damaged exactly this way. One of them is a settings file Neutrino needs for network games, so Neutrino stops before the game starts and your PS2 goes back to the browser. You didn't do anything wrong.
+
+**What to do:**
+1. On your PC, copy the `neutrino` folder from the RiptOPL zip you downloaded to a USB drive.
+2. On your PS2, copy that `neutrino` folder from the USB drive to mc1 (wLaunchELF works for this) and let it replace the old one.
+3. For now, don't copy it straight from the PC share over the network. That can damage the files again.
+
+**The UDPFS side:** the next RiptOPL build fixes the network driver, so files RiptOPL reads over UDPFS arrive complete. That may also be why some of your covers didn't show on UDPFS.
+
+Let me know if your games start after you copy the folder again.
diff --git a/notes/ISSUE-1010-FIX-COMMENT-DRAFT.md b/notes/ISSUE-1010-FIX-COMMENT-DRAFT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7d48caa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/notes/ISSUE-1010-FIX-COMMENT-DRAFT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+Good news: I found the problem and the fix is merged. No more tests needed from you, thank you for your patience!
+
+**What was wrong:** before each UDPFS game, RiptOPL updates a small Neutrino settings file on your memory card (`neutrino/config/bsd-udpfs.toml`). On a memory card, that update could leave a few broken characters at the end of the file. After that, Neutrino could not read the file, so every game went back to the PS2 browser. This was a RiptOPL bug, not something you did.
+
+**What you need to do:** just update RiptOPL to **v1.2.0 Beta 4102 or newer** (the normal rolling download). Nothing else.
+
+The new version repairs the broken file on your memory card by itself the first time you start a game. You don't need to delete or copy anything, and you can keep Neutrino on mc1 like you have it now.
+
+If a game still goes back to the browser after updating, please tell me here.
