+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>P1</code></td><td><b>Xbox One and Series controllers over USB</b></td><td>Wired Xbox controllers through a new IOP driver. RiptOPL supports DualShock 3, DualShock 4 and DualSense. v5.0 adds Xbox 360 pads, the gap tracked as <a href="#modular-pademu">MP1</a>.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/tree/main/modules/xboxusb">modules/xboxusb</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>P2</code></td><td><b>Download covers from the PS2</b></td><td>Fetches missing covers, or refreshes all of them, over the network from the console.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/blob/main/src/opl.c">src/opl.c</a><br><a href="https://irfanlesnar.github.io/PS2-Launcher-Manager/">PS2-Launcher-Manager</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>P3</code></td><td><b>One games list across every device</b></td><td>A single Games list combining every connected source, part of its console-style interface. v5.0 adds sorting that list by device.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/blob/main/src/opl.c">src/opl.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>P4</code></td><td><b>Hold SELECT to leave a game</b></td><td>Holding SELECT for 7&ndash;10 seconds in a game returns to the launcher, an alternative to the multi-button <a href="igr.html">in-game reset</a> combo.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/blob/main/ee_core/src/padhook.c">ee_core/src/padhook.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>P5</code></td><td><b>Launch transition animation</b></td><td>An animated transition as a game starts. OPL-Evolution adapted it too.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/blob/main/src/opl.c">src/opl.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>P6</code></td><td><b>More USB controllers: Steam Controller, Shanwan PS3 clones, ANT Esports GP300</b></td><td>v5.0 lists the Steam Controller (2026), Shanwan PS3 clone pads and the ANT Esports GP300 Pro V2 wireless controller. RiptOPL's USB driver accepts only Sony's DualShock 3, DualShock 4 and DualSense IDs and has no clone-specific handling.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Irfanlesnar/PS2-Launcher/releases/tag/v5.0.0">v5.0.0 release notes</a></td></tr>
