+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">PS2-Launcher v5.0 overlap</div>
+v5.0's Files tab (browse devices, copy, paste and delete files, launch games and ELFs) overlaps <a href="#boliviaos">B1</a>,
+and its Xbox 360 support overlaps <a href="#modular-pademu">MP1</a>; those receive no new P-series IDs. Already in RiptOPL:
+MMCE storage, the full in-game resolution list (RiptOPL also has 720p, 1080i and 1080p), the IGR Path setting, per-game
+OSD language, and multitap emulation for extra players (set up in <a href="pademu.html">Controller Emulation</a>
+rather than assigned automatically). Its new SMB IP options are not itemised; RiptOPL already offers DHCP or
+a static address with gateway and DNS, and reaches the server by IP or name. The faster Apps tab is a performance change,
+not a capability.</div>
