+<h2 id="orbit">ORBIT</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher">danielnuld/ps2-launcher</a> by
+<a href="https://github.com/danielnuld">danielnuld</a> &mdash; a standalone PS2 launcher built around Neutrino.
+Audited against <a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/commit/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d"><code>d015baf7</code></a>
+and RiptOPL <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/dc6206f60bf8175d88946c175e839d59ada9d9ab"><code>rebuild/main@dc6206f6</code></a>.
+Re-checked on 2026-10-06 against <a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/releases/tag/v1.0.2">v1.0.2</a>:
+v1.0.1 and v1.0.2 are fixes (a 1024-game limit, cover loading, DNS with DHCP, and MemCard PRO 2 game IDs on every
+launch, which RiptOPL already sends), so they add no entries. OR1 and OR2 have since shipped in RiptOPL (see <a href="#notes">Notes</a>).
+These are capability differences, not claims that every game or storage device has passed on a console.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>OR3</code></td><td><b>RetroAchievements telemetry with Neutrino games</b></td><td>ORBIT passes a watch list to its Neutrino fork and loads an in-game agent that streams watched memory to xeRAbora. <b>2026-10-15 update: implemented, conditional.</b> RiptOPL's complete RA kit now bundles ORBIT's RA Neutrino runtime and supports compatible local launches; UDPFS/UDPBD telemetry is experimental and requires saved watches, static IP and a known companion. Ordinary Neutrino/Ember installs do not gain this automatically. See <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/923">PR #923</a> and <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/docs/RETROACHIEVEMENTS.md">current limitations</a>. ORBIT reports one real-console UDPFS/Neutrino session with snapshots; that does not establish broad game compatibility.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/launcher.c">launcher.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/third_party/neutrino-igr/ra.c">Neutrino agent</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/docs/phase17-results.md">console report</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OR4</code></td><td><b>Browse achievement titles and progress on the console</b></td><td>The selected game's panel lists individual achievement titles, descriptions, points and earned state. <b>2026-10-15 update: implemented in the RA interface.</b> RiptOPL now has console achievement browsing with titles, points, descriptions and filters using the xerabora/Caduceus companion. The exact ORBIT presentation differs, and physical runtime behavior still varies by transport. See <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/916">PR #916</a>. ORBIT's phase-16b report records host/PCSX2 checks for this panel and leaves the console check open.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/launcher.c">launcher.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/achievements.c">achievements.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/docs/phase16b-results.md">phase-16b evidence</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OR5</code></td><td><b>Companion catalog for UDPFS games</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>An HTTP companion service lists titles, paths, IDs and precomputed RA hashes for games whose ISO data is served through UDPFS, without mounting UDPFS in the menu. RiptOPL already lists UDPFS files through its filesystem driver and has a separate <code>games.csv</code> catalog for HTTP streaming; this row tracks ORBIT's distinct UDPFS catalog workflow, not a missing ability to list or launch UDPFS games.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/launcher.c">launcher.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/tools/orbit_catalog.py">orbit_catalog.py</a><br><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/docs/phase17-results.md">console report</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">ORBIT overlap and validation</div>
+ORBIT's on-console HTTPS cover fetch overlaps <a href="#ps2-launcher">P2</a>; its combined-source library and animated launch screen overlap P3 and P5; and its resumable Neutrino in-game menu overlaps the capability tracked in <a href="#project-titan">T3</a> and <a href="#luna">LU8</a>. ORBIT's <a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/ps2-launcher/blob/d015baf7e4c004fa5db6964dc6bedd16484ea45d/docs/phase13-results.md">phase-13 report</a> records a menu pass in one game at 480p, with other video modes and later core builds needing separate checks. Those overlaps receive no new OR-series IDs. ORBIT's standard-source and Neutrino per-game options, PS1/Apps paths and two interface languages also have RiptOPL counterparts.</div>
