+<h2 id="e2opl">E2OPL</h2>
+<p><a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/e2opl/">E2OPL</a> &mdash; a historical OPL branch whose defining change was
+read-only EXT2 support for USB storage. Its published README requires the EXT2 partition to be first, uses 4096-byte
+blocks and supports ISO files rather than USBExtreme splitting.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>X1</code></td><td><b>EXT2 USB filesystem support</b></td><td>Loads PS2 ISO images from a read-only EXT2 USB partition, avoiding FAT32's 4 GiB file limit and fragmentation requirement. RiptOPL supports FAT/exFAT-style BDM filesystems but has no EXT2 filesystem driver, so this remains a distinct storage-format capability even though exFAT solves most of the same practical problem today.</td><td><a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/e2opl/">SourceForge project</a><br><a href="https://sourceforge.net/p/e2opl/code/HEAD/tree/trunk/README">source README</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+
+<h2 id="modular-pademu">Open PS2 Loader Modular PADEMU</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/belek666/Open-PS2-Loader/tree/modularPademu">belek666/Open-PS2-Loader <code>modularPademu</code></a>
+&mdash; a 2020 experimental branch that split PADEMU into controller-specific modules. DS3/DS4 overlap modern OPL,
+and its Xbox One USB path overlaps <a href="#ps2-launcher">P1</a>; the two controller classes below still have no
+equivalent module in RiptOPL.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>MP1</code></td><td><b>Xbox 360 controllers over USB</b> <span class="pill">Historical</span></td><td>A dedicated wired-Xbox-360 module recognizes Microsoft and several third-party VID/PID pairs, translates reports to DualShock 2 input and drives LEDs/rumble. RiptOPL has no <code>xbox360usb</code> PADEMU module.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/belek666/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/modularPademu/modules/pademu/xbox360usb/xbox360usb.c">xbox360usb.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>MP2</code></td><td><b>Generic USB HID gamepads</b> <span class="pill">Historical</span></td><td>A generic HID module parses a USB gamepad's HID report descriptor and maps buttons, hats and axes into the emulated DS2 report instead of requiring a controller-specific driver. This is separate from Titan's keyboard/mouse support and BoliviaOS's USB keyboard support.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/belek666/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/modularPademu/modules/pademu/hidusb/hidusb.c">hidusb.c</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">Modular PADEMU status</div>
+These are historical source capabilities, not claims of current RiptOPL-era hardware validation. The branch head is
+<a href="https://github.com/belek666/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/66b935422bc83619fc30187418cbf189c375002a"><code>66b93542</code></a>
+from 2020. Its Xbox One USB module is not counted separately because modern Xbox One / Series USB support is already P1.
+</div>
