+<h2 id="rrve">RRVE / exaconn OPL wheel work</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader">exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader</a> &mdash; the repository previously
+listed here as the wOPL Ridge Racer V Edition. Its current 2026 source has moved beyond that label and contains
+Logitech wheel work on <code>master</code>, plus a companion
+<a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/tree/Driving-Force-2-negCon-Edition"><code>Driving-Force-2-negCon-Edition</code></a>
+branch. The entry below describes the code that actually exists now rather than inferring features from the old RRVE name.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>RR1</code></td><td><b>USB Driving Force wheel with negCon presentation</b> <span class="pill">Experimental</span></td><td>The DS34 USB path recognizes Logitech wheel devices, parses wheel/pedal reports and applies a spring/auto-centering command. The companion branch presents that wheel through the PS1 <code>negCon</code> protocol (<code>0x23</code>) instead of only emulating a normal DS2, which is useful to titles designed around negCon-style analog steering. RiptOPL's DS34 USB driver has no Logitech <code>dfreport</code> / negCon path.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/3ab34d2028e3da9592b99b4681a7cdb324e3a070">Logitech definitions</a><br><a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/e70e6cbddf39a68497c28b302d19695ee2ce753a">auto-centering</a><br><a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/tree/Driving-Force-2-negCon-Edition">negCon branch</a></td></tr>
