+<h3 id="http-backed-smb-audit">PS2SMB: HTTP range content presented as SMB files</h3>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/forbenaj/ps2smb">forbenaj/ps2smb</a> is a Python proof of concept: OPL still connects to a conventional SMB share, but the SMB server's file handles are backed by remote HTTP(S) ISO sources. Its source includes an Impacket SMB1/SMB2 virtual-file interception layer, a persistent chunk cache and a local admin/status endpoint. This is **not** RiptOPL's existing native HTTP game-streaming protocol and **not** ordinary local-file SMB hosting in PS2-Servers.</p>
+<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Difference</th><th>Scope, risk and status</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td><code>SM1</code></td><td><b>Read-only virtual SMB share with HTTP-range sparse fetching</b></td><td>Remote file HEAD/Range probe, exact <code>206 Partial Content</code> reads, 8-MiB disk-backed cache chunks, sequential prefetch and SMB1 file-open/read hooks. The PS2 sees a regular SMB game image; an HTTPS source must support reliable ranges. <b>Upstream explicitly still requests a real-console game test</b>; software tests do not establish consistent gameplay latency, FMV streaming or resets. This is a <b>PS2-Servers host-side candidate</b>, not a missing RiptOPL transport. Before adoption, enforce URL allowlists, bounded cache/storage, timeouts, content consistency and lawful user-supplied remote sources; avoid shipping arbitrary remote-catalog access by default.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/forbenaj/ps2smb/blob/4ddd3fd96c77a4a20adaad84f7f070b0eddd28a8/ps2smb/smb/server.py">SMB hooks</a> · <a href="https://github.com/forbenaj/ps2smb/blob/4ddd3fd96c77a4a20adaad84f7f070b0eddd28a8/ps2smb/remote.py">HTTP range</a> · <a href="https://github.com/forbenaj/ps2smb/blob/4ddd3fd96c77a4a20adaad84f7f070b0eddd28a8/ps2smb/cache.py">persistent cache</a></td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
+
+<h3 id="ps5-opl-audit">Daniel's PS5-style Open PS2 Loader fork</h3>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader/tree/master/themes/PS5">danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader</a> extends the standard OPL theme element ABI; this is **not** evidence that RiptOPL lacks basic cover art, theme switching, Coverflow, per-game backgrounds or game-details screens. Unlike a configuration-only theme, the source implements new <code>FrostedPanel</code>, <code>CardShelf</code>, <code>CoverWallpaper</code> and <code>ItemTitle</code> primitives in the runtime. RiptOPL's current theme element vocabulary lacks those exact elements; porting the entire older fork would risk losing modern RiptOPL driver, library and achievements work.</p>
+<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Difference</th><th>Scope and evidence</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td><code>DN1</code></td><td><b>GS framebuffer-based frosted-glass blur panel</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>Blur render targets are sized for GS frame/texture stride alignment and composite a sampled backdrop behind a theme-controlled transparent panel. This is a discrete compositing operation, not simply a semitransparent rectangle. Require per-video-mode VRAM/GS fallback and profiling (480i/480p/other RiptOPL modes, music and background art active) before any hardware claim.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/fca8fcb03e8ca366a49123cd85e7ec43d39697f9/src/rmblur.c">GS blur render chain</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/fca8fcb03e8ca366a49123cd85e7ec43d39697f9/src/themes.c">FrostedPanel element</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>DN2</code></td><td><b>CardShelf + animated CoverWallpaper + selected ItemTitle primitives</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>Horizontal selection swaps navigation axes; shelf cards lift/scale the focused cover while crossfading wallpaper responds to the selection. <code>ItemTitle</code> exposes the readable game title separately from serial-ID <code>ItemText</code>. RiptOPL already implements alternative layouts, Coverflow and display-title logic, so this row counts only the distinct reusable theme-element API/presentation, <em>not</em> three missing game-library abilities. Front-end performance, texture lifetime and HD-video constraints need hardware validation.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/fca8fcb03e8ca366a49123cd85e7ec43d39697f9/src/themes.c">theme element implementation</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danielnuld/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/fca8fcb03e8ca366a49123cd85e7ec43d39697f9/themes/PS5/conf_theme.cfg">theme configuration</a></td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
