+<h2 id="notes">Notes</h2>
+<p><b>2026-10-08 retired IDs:</b> W4 (live disc-art toggle), W5 (pad tick-wrap fix) and H1 (pointer chains) are already implemented in RiptOPL, in <code>src/themes.c</code>, <code>src/pad.c</code> and <code>ee_core/src/ra.c</code> respectively. LU1 and LU3 describe removed LUNA views from the earlier snapshot; their IDs remain reserved. OR1/OR2 remain retired, with PS1 save-icon coverage now extended to VCD and Ember by PR #876.</p>
+<ul>
+  <li><b>OPHTML parity checked on 2026-09-27:</b> <a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML">OPHTML / ps2ui</a> by <a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions">coffeedevsolutions</a> (Blake Coffee), audited against <a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/commit/60810bd2ec0e2656d7425603e760ac010883f53a"><code>main@60810bd</code></a> (version 0.10.0, <code>.uib</code> format v7). While publicly titled as a web-technology UI toolkit, the source contains an embedded OPL-compatible game launcher (<code>ophtml.elf</code>) and environment. Overlapping launcher features (Neutrino no-reset launch in <code>src/elfldr_noreset.c</code>, ISO9660 SYSTEM.CNF extraction in <code>src/retrogem.c</code>, texture streaming in <code>src/texcache.c</code>, and list windowing) were excluded as existing RiptOPL parity, leaving 11 genuine code-level gaps: declarative flexbox compilation to zero-allocation C99 GS runtime, pre-resolved pairwise HarfBuzz kerning on the EE, instant 1-byte palette theme switching, runtime 2D coordinate offsets, focus subtree visibility masking with automatic D-pad bypass, automated CRT overscan &amp; multi-layer alpha contrast linter, browser-based theme simulation, static VRAM budgeting, Play! emulator CI testing, EE bus-alignment fuzzer hardening, and compiler safety ceilings.</li>
+  <li><b>LUNA parity checked on 2026-09-22:</b> <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA">LUNA</a> by <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx">darkladark</a>, audited against <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/commit/23112ecce73823b13d11d57fda0abd5968808d7c"><code>main@23112ec</code></a> and RiptOPL <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/abf14079e66ae5a5f3f943011dbe3356e2e1152b"><code>rebuild/main@abf14079</code></a>. Eight source-backed gaps survived overlap checking. LU8 tracks LUNA's Neutrino in-game return because the implementation is present and RiptOPL's Neutrino core lacks IGR; it remains marked WIP because LUNA's current README has not promoted the feature to stable status.</li>
+  <li><b>Previously awaiting variants fully audited on 2026-09-22:</b> E2OPL's historical SourceForge source; OPL Daily Build <a href="https://github.com/Jay-Jay-OPL/OPL-Daily-Builds/commit/aa531a858c583104bfd577c4715339c8ce68d534"><code>aa531a85</code></a>; Modular PADEMU <a href="https://github.com/belek666/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/66b935422bc83619fc30187418cbf189c375002a"><code>66b93542</code></a>; Grimdoomer's large-capacity branch <a href="https://github.com/grimdoomer/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/d1f51be4452074c2352931e0b9c474da9242e481"><code>d1f51be4</code></a> plus its later BDM LBA fix branch; historical uOPL <a href="https://github.com/slimpuggamer/uOPL/commit/0daf81fe035f5d29e5ca653cd8e4fe588fe9ea64"><code>0daf81fe</code></a>; X2P <a href="https://github.com/koraxial/Xbox-2-PlayStation-Emulator-AlFa/commit/160c3e18c508432323946fca9bb5cb989705f28e"><code>160c3e18</code></a>; exaconn master <a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/73a4921dee722837c18150d0c0f1a7f3675e8349"><code>73a4921d</code></a> and negCon branch <a href="https://github.com/exaconn/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/f9717f7676a6d7db588a1c042c3eaff36ec414b0"><code>f9717f76</code></a>; and Stable OPL <a href="https://github.com/mystyq/Stable-Open-PS2-Loader/commit/770d5323928ff20990d07d70a5ce266a95e0f6c4"><code>770d5323</code></a>. Six new gaps survived code comparison; three projects moved to the no-gap table.</li>
+  <li><b>Project Titan Magenta Edition parity checked on 2026-09-22:</b> audited against upstream <a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/commit/2a69c259c80e351da118cb416de1e6f0129e2816"><code>main@2a69c259</code></a> / <code>VERSION</code> 0.3.93-rc17 and RiptOPL <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/abf14079e66ae5a5f3f943011dbe3356e2e1152b"><code>rebuild/main@abf14079</code></a>. Titan's controller, Smart IGR and Store/Download documentation explicitly retains physical-target validation caveats; those rows describe source capability, not a hardware-compatibility guarantee.</li>
+  <li><b>NHDDL parity checked on 2026-09-20:</b> RiptOPL already has the visual Game ID signal used by PixelFX/RetroGEM hardware, MMCE GameID switching for SD2PSX/MemCard PRO2 on cross-device launches, remembered last-played selection with optional autostart, persistent ISO metadata caching, and global/per-game Neutrino arguments. Those are therefore not N-series gaps.</li>
+  <li><b>Already in RiptOPL, so not listed:</b> the fix from wOPL PR #435 (remember the last played game when it is
+  the first list entry), <a href="cheats.html#ps2rd-image">PS2RD cheat images (<code>.img</code>)</a>, cover art from
+  <code>ART/art.tar</code> (<a href="settings.html#display-settings">Interface settings</a>), per-game configs from
+  <code>CFG/cfg.tar</code>, cheats from <a href="cheats.html#cht-files"><code>CHT/cht.tar</code></a>, persistent TAR
+  index sidecars for all three archive kinds, the <code>&lt;name&gt;_show_run</code> theme key,
+  RetroAchievements for <a href="retroachievements.html#physical-discs">physical discs</a>, per-game OSD language,
+  virtual memory card creation, and the older USB driver that upstream PR #1752 proposes pinning.</li>
+  <li><b>Shipped since the survey:</b> Ratchet &amp; Clank 3 over SMB (was U5, from upstream PR #1761), Pro Evolution
+  Soccer 2 defaulting to Accurate Reads (was U7, see <a href="per-game-settings.html#compatibility-modes">Compatibility
+  Modes</a>) and Galician and Serbian UI languages (was U8, see <a href="languages.html#naming">Languages</a>), all in
+  <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/658">PR #658</a>; remembered per-game cheat selections
+  (was U2, from upstream PR #1748, in <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/846">PR #846</a>, see
+  <a href="cheats.html#cheat-modes">Cheat modes</a>); Create VMC on First Launch (was OR2, in
+  <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/842">PR #842</a>, see
+  <a href="settings.html#game-launching">Game Launching</a>); out-of-bounds reads checked against the real media size
+  (was U3, from upstream PR #1763, in <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/840">PR #840</a>);
+  in-game reset without the VBLANK interrupt (was U4, from upstream PR #1762, in
+  <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/841">PR #841</a>, see <a href="igr.html#limitations">In-Game
+  Reset</a>); and animated 3D save icons (was OR1, in <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/843">PR
+  #843</a>, see <a href="settings.html#artwork-settings">Artwork Settings</a>). IDs are not reused.</li>
+  <li><b>wOPL's config format:</b> wOPL moved to libconfig. RiptOPL reads and writes both formats, so files the two
+  loaders share, such as an app's <code>title.cfg</code>, keep working in both.</li>
+  <li><b>Device names:</b> RiptOPL accepts <code>usb0:</code> and <code>ata0:</code> style names for its boot path and
+  ties each launch to its device by driver name, but reads files through <code>massN:</code>. wOPL uses the typed
+  names throughout. That is a different approach rather than a missing feature, so it is not counted.</li>
+  <li><b>TAR archive status:</b> the older survey note about <code>CFG/cfg.tar</code> is obsolete. RiptOPL
+  <code>rebuild/main</code> now has one indexed/persistently cached TAR engine for <code>ART/art.tar</code>,
+  <code>CFG/cfg.tar</code> and <code>CHT/cht.tar</code>. Consequently, sOPL's TAR work is not a current gap, and an
+  archive claim is counted only when its implementation can be located in the audited source.</li>
+</ul>
+<section aria-labelledby="project-directory" class="fork-gap-section">
+<h2 id="project-directory">Alphabetical PS2 loader and companion project directory</h2>
+<p class="lead">One place to discover PS2 loaders, launchers and adjacent utilities, including projects with <em>zero confirmed missing features</em>, historical implementations, PC-side helpers, bootloaders and adjacent projects still needing closer comparison. The directory is <b>not</b> a claim that every GitHub fork is unique, maintained, safe to run or hardware-tested. All 144 entries have explicit destination links; no project is automatically a feature request.</p>
+<div class="fork-gap-note"><b>New comparison candidates (2026-10-15; no confirmed gap IDs):</b>
+<a href="https://github.com/HiroTex/OSD-XMB">OSD-XMB</a> merits priority source comparison for its plugin-driven PS1/PS2 library, on-device artwork downloads, Neutrino per-game settings, memory-card tools and device startup;
+<a href="https://www.psx-place.com/threads/xtremeeliteboot-s-dashboard-special-xmas-showcase.38959/">XEB+</a> and its <a href="https://github.com/sync-on-luma/xebplus-neutrino-loader-plugin">Neutrino plugin</a> for dashboard/device/config workflows;
+<a href="https://github.com/ps2-mmce/mmceman">MMCEMAN</a>, <a href="https://github.com/GorGylka/UDPBD-A5-V11">OpenWRT UDPBD</a> and <a href="https://github.com/retronas/retronas">RetroNAS</a> for driver/server compatibility; and
+<a href="https://oplmanager.com/">OPL Manager</a>, <a href="https://github.com/bucanero/apollo-ps2">Apollo Save Tool</a> and <a href="https://github.com/israpps/HDL-Batch-installer">HDL Batch Installer</a> for PC/console library and save workflows.
+Boot exploits, optical-disc modification and external PC tools are included as <em>references</em>, not assumed OPL features. Verify code, existing RiptOPL parity, and physical-console safety before promoting any entry to a gap.</div>
