+          "message": "build(neutrino): ship RiptOPL's i.LINK driver in the Neutrino bundle (#1018)\n\nNeutrino's in-game environment loads its own iLinkman + IEEE1394_bd_mini\nafter its IOP reboot (config/bsd-ilink.toml), the same SDK code with the\nsame post-reset login race. The required ps2dev-latest build stages\nmodules/ilink/IEEE1394_bd/IEEE1394_bd_mini.irx as its own artifact (not\nrolling/, which is published wholesale); publish-rolling replaces\nneutrino/modules/IEEE1394_bd_mini.irx with it and refuses to package if\nupstream stops shipping that file or the copy does not land.\npackage_release_app.py requires the file in ordinary packages; the RA kit\nkeeps ORBIT's Neutrino unmodified. docs/NEUTRINO.md says what changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
