+          "message": "build(pops-ilink): ship the rebuilt usbhdfsd.irx.ilink; CI proves it (#1018)\n\nRebuilt modules/bdmassault/ilink_bd_assault with its own Makefile in the\nPS2DEVPINNED container (ghcr.io/ps2dev/ps2dev@sha256:8fba50ec...): 21977\nbytes, sha256 8f9a9e4e6984a58435fe7e24e1e5832f027dc537b3274bc4220245bbe1844714.\nThe same container rebuilds the previous 21609-byte binary (9b47d90b...)\nfrom the previous source byte for byte, and CRLF and LF checkouts give\nidentical output, so the bytes are the committed source and nothing else.\n\n- Replace all three copies: modules/bdmassault/, POPS/ (what releases\n  ship) and the Example kit's root copy.\n- vcdBdmaPairSig iLink size 21609 -> 21977. A card still equipped with\n  the old driver now fails the size check, so Apply on Launch re-equips\n  it from the device's POPS/ folder.\n- New flavours job popstarter-ilink-driver rebuilds the module in that\n  container on every PR, fails unless every checked-in copy is exactly\n  that output, and uploads the build.\n- PROVENANCE.md, the module README (local changes 5-7, how to rebuild)\n  and docs/VCD.md (#1018 note; step 7 still listed the 23,452-byte\n  pre-September driver).\n\nNot tested on hardware.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
