+        {
+          "sha": "b5cf52f7d9a9418fb8c77b6b638fa0f946876ecb",
+          "message": "RA: hash PS1 images for POPS (.VCD)\n\nraHashVcd reads a VCD the way rc_hash_psx reads a PS1 disc: skip the\n1 MiB POPS header, map 2048-byte offsets onto 2352-byte MODE2 sectors,\ntake BOOT from SYSTEM.CNF (PSX.EXE if there is none), size from the\nPS-X EXE header plus 2048, MD5 of name and bytes. Directory names now\ncompare case-insensitively, as rcheevos does for both consoles.\n\nNot called yet. Host test on Blade (USA): 3e64b72f..., RA game 14491.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
+        {
+          "sha": "b8a13423296a7f476e75eff2b615ebaac578d045",
+          "message": "PS1: list POPS/*.VCD with the PS2 games and launch POPStarter\n\nThe BDM pages append every POPS/<name>.VCD at the device root, marked\n\"PS1\", with the serial read out of the image's SYSTEM.CNF. Launching\none copies POPS/POPSTARTER.ELF to XX.<name>.ELF if it is missing and\nloads it as mass:/POPS/XX.<name>.ELF: POPStarter parses its argv[0],\nand the SDK loader sets argv[0] to the path it loads. First USB device\nonly for now. The RA check hashes the VCD and asks the PC as for PS2.\n\nA new UI setting, \"PS1 and PS2 order\": mixed by name, PS2 first or\nPS1 first. The sort now compares game names, not badged text.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
+        {
+          "sha": "7458ddbfde39beb535425fbed6aaaf8f3aa4600c",
+          "message": "PS1: drop the PS1/PS2 order setting\n\nThe build with it hung in the menu on hardware, and two probes showed\nthe hang is not in the POPS/ scan. Removed: the setting, the group and\nsort-key fields on menu items, the sort by them. The sort is stock again.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
+        {
+          "sha": "a3fd53588323bb16a5fbfbb1b15fbbc0915814d7",
+          "message": "RA: name the sector source instead of a sentinel fd and a flag\n\nread_at() took a file descriptor, with -100 standing for the drive and\na global flag switching it to VCD sectors around each call. It now\ntakes a struct ra_src with the descriptor and its kind. The PS1 code\nreads SYSTEM.CNF in one place for the list and for the hash.\n\nHost test: Blade.VCD 3e64b72f... (RA 14491) and Dynasty Warriors 2\n29e392c7... (RA 19047), both unchanged. cppcheck finds nothing in the\nchanged lines.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
+        {
+          "sha": "531aad4584d65d1779b744739b81402150c7669c",
+          "message": "PS1: achievements under POPStarter\n\nA PS1 image in POPS/<name>.VCD on a block device is listed with the PS2\ngames, marked PS1, hashed the way rcheevos hashes a PS1 disc and\nlaunched through POPStarter (krHACKen r13) as mass:/POPS/XX.<name>.ELF.\nNothing of OPL runs under POPS, so the watch list travels inside\nPOPS/MODULE_9.IRX: OPL writes a copy of rapops with the IP\nconfiguration, the serial and the list in its config block, POPStarter\nloads it on the IOP after its own reset. rapops brings up DEV9, SMAP,\nthe TCP/IP stack and raudp as under a PS2 game, then starts rapull,\nwhich reads the PS1 RAM windows through sceSifGetOtherData at 60 Hz and\nhands the snapshots to raudp. The first request waits 25 seconds: one\nduring POPS's boot leaves the screen black.\n\nPOPStarter reads the game's device with its own driver. OPL puts the\nBDMAssault pair for the device on the memory card before the launch\n(mc?:/POPSTARTER/, RA_BDMA.TXT names the variant): mx4sio, ata, ilink.\nUSB stays on the built-in FAT32 driver unless \"PS1 USB drive is exFAT\"\nis on in Settings; OPL cannot tell the formats apart, and the usbexfat\npair stalls POPS on its first video from a FAT32 stick.\n\nConfirmed on hardware: Blade from a FAT32 stick and from an exFAT\ndrive, 60 snapshots a second, achievements unlock. Not done: PS1 from\nMMCE, an APA HDD or a share; a second device of the same kind. The\nMX4SIO, iLink and exFAT HDD pairs follow RiptOPL and have not been\nrun here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
+        {
+          "sha": "fa2d2e42cc76881afa914da943da303addbba928",
+          "message": "Keep the RA snapshot going when Mode 6 turns the IGR off\n\nRA_OnVblank ran only from the IGR's VBLANK_END handler, and Mode 6\nskips Install_IGR, so a game set to Mode 6 sent no telemetry at all.\nSly Cooper and the Thievius Raccoonus needs that mode: it takes the\nIGR's padOpen patch for tampering and hides collectibles (xerabora\nissue #15).\n\nUnder Mode 6 syshook now installs a handler that calls RA_OnVblank and\nnothing else: no IGR thread, no padOpen patch, no CreateThread/ExecPS2\nhooks. A reset asked for over the network has nothing to carry it out\nin that mode, so IGR_RequestReset drops it.\n\nBuilt, not run on hardware.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
+        },
