+      "body": "## Fixed\n\n- Games with a large achievement set could launch with no telemetry: the list of memory addresses arrived on the console damaged, and the console dropped it. Found on Mortal Kombat: Shaolin Monks, which watches 2679 addresses. After the fix the game streams from the first second and the achievements unlock on hardware.\n- The hardcore flag read from the Web API was wrong whenever an unlock had both dates, which a hardcore unlock always has.\n\n## Added\n\n- The rich presence line the game is sending, on the CONSOLE panel.\n- UNLOCK ON THE TV on SETTINGS: off keeps every unlock on the page and sends nothing to the console, for games whose picture the flash breaks. Saved between runs.\n- LIVE: ACHIEVEMENTS and LEADERBOARDS as two sub-tabs. ACHIEVEMENTS as the list, each row with its median unlock time, or as GRID, the badges alone as on the site. An unlocked badge wears a ring for the mode it was earned in: blue softcore, gold hardcore, half and half when both. GAME has the same LIST / GRID choice.\n\n## Removed\n\n- The cheat engine. OPL-RA no longer carries PS2RD, reads no `CHT/` files and has no cheat menu; stock OPL is for play with cheats.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hacan359/xerabora/compare/v0.1.0-alpha.17...v0.1.0-alpha.18\n\n"
