+      "body": "## Added\n\n- PS1 games through POPStarter. A `.VCD` in `POPS/` on a USB stick is listed with the PS2 games, marked PS1, and runs in Sony's PS1 emulator with the game's PS1 achievement set. Check it once with \"RA: check game support\", launch, play: the console reads the PS1 memory from the IOP and streams it as for a PS2 game. What goes in `POPS/` and what is not covered: [USAGE, \"PS1 games through POPStarter\"](https://github.com/hacan359/xerabora/blob/main/docs/USAGE.md#ps1-games-through-popstarter).\n- Settings → \"PS1 USB drive is exFAT\". POPStarter's own driver reads FAT32 only; with this on, OPL puts the BDMAssault `usbexfat` pair on the memory card before the launch and takes it off when the setting is off.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- PS1 is tested from USB, FAT32 and exFAT. MX4SIO, iLink and an exFAT HDD get their driver pair the same way but were not run here. Not covered: PS1 from an MMCE device, an APA HDD or a share. No gold flash under POPS, the unlock shows on the client's page. The telemetry starts 25 seconds after the launch.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hacan359/xerabora/compare/v0.1.0-alpha.15...v0.1.0-alpha.16\n\n"
