+      "body": "## Fixed\n\n- Some games hung about ten seconds after start, as soon as the first memory snapshot was taken. Their achievement sets read memory at addresses the console could not read in one go. Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas is one of them. Those reads work now.\n- A snapshot that arrived while the previous one was still being sent could be lost.\n- A watch list with a broken entry is refused instead of shifting every value after it.\n- Games on an SD card in the memory card slot (MX4SIO) did not boot: the driver they need now travels with the game.\n\n## Added\n\n- Pointer chains that carry an address mask are followed. Scooby-Doo! and the Spooky Swamp goes from 10 supported chains to all 71.\n- RESET CONSOLE on the LIVE page sends the console back to the loader menu, no button combo needed. Where it lands is OPL's IGR Path setting: point it at a copy of the ELF on the memory card to come back to OPL+RA.\n- The release build no longer writes hash logs to the share; the debug build keeps them.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hacan359/xerabora/compare/v0.1.0-alpha.12...v0.1.0-ManoAlpha.13\n\n"
