+      "body": "- Big achievement sets are supported: the watch list is split into chunks, so a set that did not fit in one packet now reaches the console.\n- The console shows why a set was refused (unknown game, set too big, server down) instead of a generic message, and waits longer for the answer.\n- A dump the set does not match is reported as the wrong dump.\n- Added a survey mode in the client: it counts what a set needs before you play it.\n\n- The image check failed when the client remembered another game from an earlier session.\n- A game launched from a USB stick with a stored watch list sent no telemetry: the network adapter was not powered.\n- Loading a set blocked the client for seconds and the console gave up waiting. Loading now runs in the background.\n- On Windows the client could start a second copy of itself.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hacan359/xerabora/compare/v0.1.0-alpha.10...v0.1.0-alpha.11\n\n"
