+      "body": "<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/v1.0.2-beta/media/ripps2-test-me.png\" alt=\"RIPPS2: Test me, build 102\"></p>\n\n## Kill it: RIPPS2 v1.0.2 beta (build 102)\n\n**[Download RIPPS2.elf](https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/releases/download/v1.0.2-beta/RIPPS2.elf)** (one file, about 3 MB) and put it in place of your old one. Your settings stay in your memory card's RIPPS2 save. The **[theme pack](https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2-themes/releases/latest)** has a new edition (v102: Adapt and Adapt Rx): replace your Adapt folders. RIPGRID and RIPFLOW are built in.\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/v1.0.2-beta/media/beta/01-adapt.jpg\" width=\"32%\" alt=\"Adapt: the disc over its case at real-life proportions, lined up with the list\">\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/v1.0.2-beta/media/beta/02-ripgrid-flip.jpg\" width=\"32%\" alt=\"RIPGRID: the grid raised, a case turned to its back cover\">\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/v1.0.2-beta/media/beta/04-info-page.jpg\" width=\"32%\" alt=\"Adapt's info page: the logo just above the text, the screenshots flush with it\">\n</p>\n\n### Sound\n- **No more beeping while a load is stuck.** When the music's read stalled (a drive coming back after an in-game reset, a busy card, the ripped menu music read from a drive), the PS2's sound driver ran out and played its last tenth of a second over and over. The music now fills the gap with silence until its next piece arrives.\n- **Switching away from stuck music no longer freezes the menu** for seconds while the read finishes.\n- **The console boot sound starts with the towers**, not the moment it has loaded.\n- **Adapt plays your ripped sounds** (a new theme key, `sounds=audio`), even copied over an older Adapt that shipped sounds of its own.\n\n### Every theme\n- **No info page switches the source.** Left, Right, Up and Down go through the games on every theme.\n- **Colors and More edits every theme's colours.** On RIPGRID and themes from a drive the colour rows were greyed out and the cursor skipped them. Now they change that theme's own colours, kept for it alone; Reset gives its own back.\n- **Apps show a square PS1 case by default.** Triangle on an app: **Case Shape** PS1, PS2 or Theme, kept for that app.\n- **Reflections and cased covers fade with their page**, long text slides smoothly a pixel at a time, and **About and STATUS read in RIPPS2's own type** on every theme, About's credits wrapping evenly inside the panel.\n\n### Memory Files\n- **A game started from the file browser starts its drive's games itself.** A drive opened only with START DRIVES could not launch a game until it was opened once in Storage.\n\n### Themes\n- **RIPGRID:** Standard glyphs (L3 and R3 included); the grid raised so the space above and below it match; the info page lined up, its logo just above the text; the CD player and file tree like RIPFLOW's, Launch Disc and Memory Files like RIPPS2's.\n- **RIPFLOW:** White glyphs, hints in RIPPS2 Sleek Case, badges and stars at their true shapes in one row.\n- **Adapt and Adapt Rx (edition 102):** the disc and case at real-life proportions (a 120 mm disc over a 135 x 190 mm case), lined up with the list's box; logos just above the info box (`valign=bottom`); readable hints on every page; the apps page under the category bar with a square case.\n\n**[Full changelog](https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)** | **[Watch the beta reel](https://youtu.be/LPjdK_E1jjM)** | **[Talk about it on psx-place](https://www.psx-place.com/threads/ripps2-a-ps2-front-end-in-one-elf-launch-disc-storage-memory-files.51316/)** | [RIPPCSX2](https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPCSX2/releases/latest) for seeing a theme in true 720p and 1080i\n\nBeta: keep your usual loader close by, and tell us what breaks in [the psx-place thread](https://www.psx-place.com/threads/ripps2-a-ps2-front-end-in-one-elf-launch-disc-storage-memory-files.51316/) or [an issue](https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/issues). The sound fixes especially want ears on a real console.\n"
