+          "message": "Build 105: RIPDISC, a disc to storage or files from Launch Disc\n\nAfter 4.2 s on Launch Disc a glass panel offers RIPDISC for a disc it can\nrip; SELECT held 4.2 s opens a confirm step with the size and the place,\nthen START rips. PS2 games go to an ISO in a drive's CD or DVD folder (1 GB\nparts and ul.cfg when over 4 GB on a drive that may be FAT32), PS1 games to\na BIN and CUE for Ember. Audio CDs and DVD videos go through Memory Files:\nRIPPED on the clipboard, PASTE in the folder picked, an audio CD's folder\nthen named on the keyboard. AUDIO and MEDIA get a README.txt, and every\n.ogg or .wav in AUDIO is music whatever its name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
