+          "message": "Build 105: the rip's time before START, learned per storage; RIPDISC in 33 languages\n\nThe confirm step says how long the rip will take: a careful guess for the\nkind of storage and disc until a rip has measured this console, then what\nthat rip really ran at, kept in the settings (ripdisc_kbs_<storage>_<cd|dvd>).\nThe running estimate shows hours past 90 minutes. Lab: POINIES POIN ripped\nfrom PCSX2's drive to a fresh exFAT HDD image is byte for byte the source\n(md5 7e7a1db3...). RIPDISC's 38 new strings are translated in every language.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
