+          "message": "Build 108: RIPSHOT, screenshots from the in-game menu; the menu silent and on by default; SCRn\n\nSCREENSHOT is the in-game menu's third choice: the frame on screen when the\nmenu opened, read back from GS memory by ee_core, written over plain SIF DMA\n(no RPC while the game is paused) to the game's roll in MEDIA/RIPSHOT on a\nBDM drive (USB, exFAT HDD, MX4SIO, iLink), 6 slots a game, a blank roll kept\nready. ART, MEDIA or BOTH, with the names the files will have; SAVE fades the\nmenu off, KEEP / DELETE. Developing to 8-bit palette PNGs (median cut, ART at\n250 x 188, MEDIA full size): Manual from the roll pages in Memory Files (VIEW,\nACTIONS), or Auto in the background. The menu is silent (SPU2 hushed, every\nvoice held) and RESUME puts the frame under the panel back.\n\nThe menu is on by default (a one-time switch for older configs) with its own\nsettings page (In-Game Menu, RIPSHOT, Develop Shots), each choice with its own\nhint; disabled settings rows read dimmed. The SCRn theme key shows every shot\nin turn (boxes one shot apart, slides the next shot each round): RIPPS2's info\npage, RIPGRID and RIPFLOW use it. MEDIA's README explains RIPSHOT.\n\nAlso: the IOPRP image device is iprp (games hung in PCSX2 with its host\nfilesystem on), the menu switches GSM's data breakpoint off while open, a\npicture taller than the TV raster stops at 480 / 576 lines, the menu's stack\nand font sit after the modules. Translated in every language. CI uploads\nee_core.map with the symbols.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
