+          "message": "Build 109: MMCE boots fast, Save Settings To, page titles clear of their line\n\nFrom testers (10/19-10/20). MMCE: a card's game list is kept on the card\n(RIPPS2.LST beside CD and DVD): at boot the games show from it at once, then\nthe card is read again in the background and the list follows what changed.\nThe scan pauses after each entry, and a frame after each disc read, so the\npads keep working (a tester: 180 games took about 5 minutes to list, with\nnothing to press). Settings > General > Save Settings To: Memory Card (as\nbefore), Internal HDD (a RIPPS2 folder on the exFAT HDD, else the APA HDD's\nOPL partition, read first through the Custom Settings Path redirect) or Custom\nPath, each choice with its hint. A page's title row is taller, so the line\nunder it no longer cuts the letters. Translated in every language. RiptOPL's\nscan harness stubs DelayThread for the host test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
