+          "message": "Build 109 hotfix: Internal HDD is saved by its type (ata0:/RIPPS2), not by its mass slot\n\nFound in the reel takes: after Save Settings To > Internal HDD on the exFAT\nHDD, config.path held mass0:/RIPPS2 and the next boot froze. An untyped\nmassN: settings path makes the boot walk every transport (USB, MX4SIO,\nthen iLink and ATA; iLinkman hangs PCSX2) before the HDD answers, and a\nUSB stick can take the slot number. Internal HDD now saves ata0:/RIPPS2\n(its RIPPS2 folder made first, since the typed resolver finds the drive by\nit), config.path keeps a typed BDM path's own spelling, and build 109's\nfirst spelling still reads as Internal HDD and is rewritten on the next\nsave.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
