+          "message": "Build 110: every source lists at once, Save Settings To on every drive\n\nThe user (10/21): speed every source up, and save settings to USB or any\nother drive RiptOPL can read them from. Build 109's MMCE card list is now\nevery source's (supportbase.c sbSnap*): the list read last time is kept on\nthe source as RIPPS2.LST, shown the moment the source answers, and the\nsource is read again on its next idle pass. MMCE, every BDM drive (USB,\nexFAT HDD, MX4SIO, iLink) and SMB use it; SMB joins the idle poll until\nread, since its timed rescans need Automatic Refresh. An MX4SIO scan pauses\nfor the pads as an MMCE one does. The APA HDD's own list cache is on by\ndefault (once for older configs) and checked against the APA table on the\nnext idle pass. Save Settings To: Memory Card, Internal HDD, USB Drive,\nMX4SIO, iLink, MMCE, Custom Path, each drive by its type with its RIPPS2\nfolder made first; MMCE loads its driver for the settings at boot. A drive\nit cannot find is said in a message box (Settings pages run their own\ndialog loop, which draws no toast). The info page asks for the size of a\ngame the d-pad reaches (it read 0 MiB). RiptOPL's BDM harnesses know the\ndrive's list. Translated in every language.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
