ripps2disc.c\n+- en: '%s is already there. Replace it?'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: '%u MB'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2hdd.c\n+- en: '%u.%02u GB'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: A BIN and CUE for Ember, in the PS1 games list.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: A FOLDER YOU PICK IN MEMORY FILES\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: A game rips to a USB drive, the exFAT HDD, MX4SIO or iLink, and none is started. Connect one, then open Storage once.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: A memory card is far too small for a disc. Paste it on a USB drive, the HDD or an MMCE card.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ABOUT %d H %02d MIN\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ABOUT %d H %02d MIN LEFT\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ABOUT %d MIN\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ABOUT %d MIN LEFT\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ADD THIS GAME TO YOUR STORAGE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ADD THIS MEDIA TO YOUR FILES\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: ANOTHER DRIVE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: AUDIO CD   %d TRACKS   %u:%02u\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: CONFIRM\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: DRIVE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2files.c\n+  - ripps2status.c\n+- en: DVD VIDEO\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2ui.c\n+- en: HDD (exFAT)\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2files.c\n+- en: HOLD\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: LESS THAN A MINUTE LEFT\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: Media rips to a USB drive, the HDD or an MMCE card, and none is started. Connect one, then open Storage once.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: 'Only a DVD video you made yourself: a bought film is copy protected, and the drive will not read it.'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: 'Over 4 GB: saved as 1 GB parts with ul.cfg, as Open PS2 Loader does, since a FAT32 drive holds 4 GB a file.'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: PS1 GAME\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2ui.c\n+- en: PS2 GAME\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2ui.c\n+- en: READING THE DISC\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2ui.c\n+- en: READY\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: RIPDISC could not read what is on the disc. Clean it, put it back and try again.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: RIPDISC found no VIDEO_TS folder it can read on this DVD.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: RIPPS2 cannot read this game's ID, which its 1 GB parts are named by. Rip it to the internal exFAT HDD instead.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: Ripped as %d parts of 1 GB with ul.cfg on the drive. It is in your games list.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: Ripped to %s as a BIN and CUE. It is in the PS1 games list, played with Ember.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: Ripped to %s. It is in your games list.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: SIZE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: Stop the rip? What it has written so far is removed.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: TIME\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: TO\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: The disc in the drive is not the one on the clipboard. Hold SELECT on LAUNCH DISC again.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: 'The rip stopped: the drive could not take more. Check it has room and is not write protected. Nothing was kept.'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: 'The rip stopped: the drive would not read the disc. A bought DVD film is copy protected and cannot be ripped; a scratched or dirty disc can also stop it. Nothing was kept.'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: 'The rip stopped: the drive would not read the disc. Clean it, put it back and try again. Nothing was kept.'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: This game is already on the drive as split parts. Delete it in Storage first to rip it again.\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+- en: USB DRIVE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2files.c\n+- en: iLINK DRIVE\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2disc.c\n+  - ripps2files.c\n - en: ASPECT\n   in:\n   - ripps2edit.c\n@@ -1388,6 +1554,9 @@ strings:\n - en: '%d FOLDERS AND CONTENTS'\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n+- en: '%d FOLDERS, %d FOUND'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2files.c\n - en: '%s BYTES'\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1464,13 +1633,10 @@ strings:\n - en: DELETED\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n+  - ripps2shot.c\n - en: DONE\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n-- en: DRIVE\n-  in:\n-  - ripps2files.c\n-  - ripps2status.c\n - en: DRIVES STARTED\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1531,9 +1697,6 @@ strings:\n - en: HDD (OPL HOME)\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n-- en: HDD (exFAT)\n-  in:\n-  - ripps2files.c\n - en: HDD MANAGER\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1550,9 +1713,6 @@ strings:\n - en: IN USE\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n-- en: INSTALLER\n-  in:\n-  - ripps2files.c\n - en: IS ALREADY HERE (%d MORE TO GO). REPLACE IT?\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1571,9 +1731,6 @@ strings:\n - en: MARK ALL\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n-- en: MC EXPLOIT\n-  in:\n-  - ripps2files.c\n - en: MEMORY CARD %c\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1623,7 +1780,7 @@ strings:\n - en: NOT FOUND\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n-- en: No installer found. Put your memory card exploit installer ELF (FreeMcBoot, OpenTuna, wLaunchELF R3Z...) in APPS on a memory card or USB drive, then choose this again.\n+- en: Nothing named \"%s\" on the drives listed. START DRIVES in the drive list starts the rest.\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n - en: 'OFF'\n@@ -1636,6 +1793,7 @@ strings:\n - en: OPEN\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n+  - ripps2shot.c\n - en: ORBIT SETTINGS\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1714,6 +1872,9 @@ strings:\n - en: RIP 3D ICON\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n+- en: RIPPED\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2files.c\n - en: RUN\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n@@ -1726,10 +1887,20 @@ strings:\n - en: Run %s?\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n+- en: SEARCH\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2files.c\n+- en: 'SEARCH: %s   %d FOUND'\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2files.c\n+- en: SEARCHING\n+  in:\n+  - ripps2files.c\n - en: SELECT\n   in:\n   - ripps2files.c\n   - ripps2ra.c\n+  - ripps2shot.c\n   - ripps2status.c\n - en: SETTINGS\n   in:\n@@ -1749,6 +1920,9 @@ strings:\n - en: Startin