+        "message": "PS1: achievements under POPStarter\n\nA PS1 image in POPS/<name>.VCD on a block device is listed with the PS2\ngames, marked PS1, hashed the way rcheevos hashes a PS1 disc and\nlaunched through POPStarter (krHACKen r13) as mass:/POPS/XX.<name>.ELF.\nNothing of OPL runs under POPS, so the watch list travels inside\nPOPS/MODULE_9.IRX: OPL writes a copy of rapops with the IP\nconfiguration, the serial and the list in its config block, POPStarter\nloads it on the IOP after its own reset. rapops brings up DEV9, SMAP,\nthe TCP/IP stack and raudp as under a PS2 game, then starts rapull,\nwhich reads the PS1 RAM windows through sceSifGetOtherData at 60 Hz and\nhands the snapshots to raudp. The first request waits 25 seconds: one\nduring POPS's boot leaves the screen black.\n\nPOPStarter reads the game's device with its own driver. OPL puts the\nBDMAssault pair for the device on the memory card before the launch\n(mc?:/POPSTARTER/, RA_BDMA.TXT names the variant): mx4sio, ata, ilink.\nUSB stays on the built-in FAT32 driver unless \"PS1 USB drive is exFAT\"\nis on in Settings; OPL cannot tell the formats apart, and the usbexfat\npair stalls POPS on its first video from a FAT32 stick.\n\nConfirmed on hardware: Blade from a FAT32 stick and from an exFAT\ndrive, 60 snapshots a second, achievements unlock. Not done: PS1 from\nMMCE, an APA HDD or a share; a second device of the same kind. The\nMX4SIO, iLink and exFAT HDD pairs follow RiptOPL and have not been\nrun here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
