+          "message": "fix(ilink): log back in after an IOP reset; offer only a ready drive (#1018)\n\ni.LINK games listed on every core, Ember booted, and native OPL (PS2\nlogo, then nothing), Neutrino and POPSTARTER did not. Ember is the only\ncore that never resets the IOP.\n\nps2sdk's IEEE1394_bd never logs out (SBP2_LOGOUT_REQUEST is defined but\nnever sent) and an IOP reset ends it without warning, so the next driver\nfinds the drive still holding the old exclusive login for its SBP-2\nreconnect hold: 2^0 = 1 s for the RECONNECT(0) every login here asks\nfor, longer on bridges that round it up. It tried 5 LOGINs 200 ms apart\n(~0.8 s), inside that hold, and only the next bus reset retries, which a\nrunning game never causes: the device never attached and CDVDMAN waited\nforever.\n\n- initConfigureSBP2Device: keep asking every 200 ms for up to 5 s of\n  elapsed time (a time budget, so slow refusals cannot stretch it).\n- scsi_warmup: TEST UNIT READY at most 300 times, 100 ms apart (30 s for\n  a cold 3.5\" drive); a block length of 0 is a failure.\n- scsi_connect: publish the device only after a successful warm-up; a\n  failed attempt frees its slot for the next bus reset.\n\nVendored as modules/ilink/IEEE1394_bd (ORIGIN.txt: pin, local changes);\nthe Makefile embeds this build, full or mini, instead of the SDK's.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
