+          "message": "feat(theme): make PSBBN Flow match the PSBBN-DP Game Collection\n\nThe built-in <PSBBN Flow> only borrowed the Collection fan: a plain blue wash, a\nlarge portrait cover, flat covers spread across the screen, the title and count\nin the bottom-left, and no selection highlight. It now follows the PSBBN\nDefinitive Project's Game Collection, measured from CosmicScale's published\nvideos (no PSBBN code or artwork):\n\n- black header and button-hint bands with thin rules, a blue nebula stage\n  (new 8-bit 160x120 psbbn_bg texture, filtered up) and a still star field\n- the page list where PSBBN lists Collection and Disc, with the stacked\n  Collection panel outline behind it\n- a rounded square focal cover (art cropped to its centre square) with PSBBN's\n  soft white rim; title above it, n/N count under its lower right corner\n- a tail of covers turned away into the distance, drawn in perspective strips\n  with perspective-correct art, darker and fading toward the far end\n- the outgoing cover swells toward the viewer and fades; title and count hide\n  while covers move and return when they settle\n\nDrawing uses rmDrawTriangles plus a blended variant; 24-bit art fades through\nthe GS fixed blend factor because it has no alpha of its own. Per frame this\nis under 200 triangles. The 25-frame cubic glide from #733/#977 is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
