+          "message": "fix(pops-ilink): log back in after POPSTARTER's IOP reset (#1018)\n\nPOPSTARTER resets the IOP and loads its i.LINK driver, usbhdfsd.irx.ilink\n(modules/bdmassault/ilink_bd_assault: an older ps2sdk IEEE1394_bd plus\niLinkman), from the memory card. That driver never logs out of the drive\n(SBP2_LOGOUT_REQUEST is defined but never sent), so after the reset the\ndrive still holds the previous driver's exclusive login for its SBP-2\nreconnect hold: 1 s for the RECONNECT(0) every login asks for, longer on\nbridges that round it up. It tried 5 LOGINs 200 ms apart (~0.8 s),\ninside that hold, and only the next bus reset retries, which POPSTARTER\nnever causes.\n\nSame three changes as OPL's own copy of the driver (PR #1022), with the\nsame constants and \"RiptOPL\" markers:\n\n- initConfigureSBP2Device: keep asking every 200 ms for up to 5 s of\n  elapsed time (GetSystemTime/SysClock2USec, already imported).\n- scsi_warmup: TEST UNIT READY at most 300 times, 100 ms apart; a block\n  length of 0 is a failure (the capacity printf divided by it). This\n  older driver has no READ CAPACITY(16) path to guard.\n- scsi_connect: offer the drive to BDM only after a successful warm-up;\n  a failed attempt frees its slot for the next bus reset.\n\nThe cdvdman removal and everything else in the driver are unchanged.\ntest_ilink_bd_assault_reset.py compiles the real scsi.c and the login\nfunction against simulated drives and a simulated clock; on the\nprevious sources it fails 11 checks and crashes on block length 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
