+            "email": "109461996+NathanNeurotic@users.noreply.github.com",
+            "date": "2026-10-21T05:58:40Z"
+          },
+          "message": "fix(bdma): name an older release's device POPS/ pair instead of a card write error\n\nA launch equip copied whatever usbd.irx.<mode> + usbhdfsd.irx.<mode> pair it\nfound first, then checked the card pair's sizes against vcdBdmaPairSig. A\ndevice POPS/ folder still holding an older release's pair (the 21609-byte\nusbhdfsd.irx.ilink after #1024) was copied on every launch, failed that\ncheck, and toasted \"Error writing the BDMA modules to the memory card\".\n\nThe launch equips (vcdEnsureBdmaForLaunch, the USB fat32/exFAT dialog and\nAPA __common) now measure each candidate pair before copying -- by reading\nit through on MMCE, which has no SEEK_END -- pass over a pair that is not\nthis release's, and keep searching the same seek order (custom dir, boot\nPOPS/, game device, other UDPFS sources, __common). With only an older pair\nfound they copy nothing, leave the card as it is, and show the new\nBDMA_ERR_OLD toast. The launch still goes ahead. The Settings page's manual\nequip is unchanged: it installs the pair the user chose.\n\nHost test test_bdma_stale_pair.py compiles the real equip and launch code;\nagainst the old source every stale case shows BDMA_ERR_IO after 4 card\ncopies. Not hardware-tested.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
