+        "message": "Theme wallpapers: a global one and one per system\n\nA background block can set `wallpaper` (PNG, JPEG or WebP, at most 16 MB)\nand `fit` (cover or stretch), drawn over the corners by the background\nlayer. The theme's shows on the systems grid and the virtual systems, a\nsystem's own while its games are shown, cross-fading with the look.\n\nWallpapers are decoded by Godot on the thread pool, scaled to fit\n2560x1080 (the 3D the background goes through is at most 1080 high), and\nat most three are kept. A system's is fetched ahead once its card has\nbeen focused for 0.15 s. The item shader reads them only while a grid\nfades, so items still fade exactly into what's behind them.\n\nOn the export, PS2's 60 s scroll with its wallpaper on screen: GPU\n0.18 -> 0.21 ms, frames, hitches and allocation unchanged, start-up\nwithin the spread, textures +16 MB for two wallpapers\n(docs/perf/wallpapers.md).\n\nGenerated with Claude Code under company AI usage policy",
