+        "message": "A theme switch frees the models the new theme doesn't use\n\nSwitching from Console to Slab kept Console's video memory until a\nrestart: models stayed for the session, and a dropped C# wrapper keeps\nits native object until its finaliser runs, which SustainedLowLatency\ncan put off indefinitely.\n\n- ModelLoader.ReleaseUnused disposes every unused model's mesh, textures\n  and clips and frees its node tree once the grids hold the new\n  templates (per-game models are left to ReleasePerGame).\n- ItemGrid.SetTemplates disposes the old materials and MultiMeshes; the\n  warm-up's go when it ends; the parked details ModelView drops its model.\n- A second after a switch, a background full collection releases the\n  textures and arrays held by SetShaderParameter's Variant disposers.\n\nConsole -> Slab now lands at 318-326 MB of Godot video memory (a fresh\nSlab start: 295.7 MB) instead of 468.8 MB, steady over four round trips;\nthe same on Vulkan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
