+        "message": "An All games card joins Favourites and Recently played\n\nEvery visible game of every enabled system in one list, third at the start\nof the systems grid (id all_games), in [display] games_sort's order. Each\ngame keeps its own system's template and shows its system's name. The list\nis cached like a system's and read again when the sort changes or a game\nends under a play-based sort; its subtitle counts the library's games.\n\nCore: GetAllGamesAsync (a system's sorted query without the system\ncondition) and GetAllGameMediaAsync (every game's media by kind in one\nquery, instead of chunks of 500 ids).\n\nThemes give it a card and logo as the other two ([systems.all_games],\nlogos/all_games.*). Slab's is ES-DE's all-games collection image, supplied\nby the owner; tools/slab-logos.py renames auto-allgames. The scroll bench\ntakes --bench-system=all_games.\n\nScrolling the 14,215 synthetic games end to end matches PS2's 10,000\n(export, Slab, 3 runs each): scroll p99 16.98-17.00 ms against\n16.97-17.00, no hitches, 96 B main-thread allocation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
