+        "message": "Choose SteamGridDB's art in manual matching\n\nChoosing a SteamGridDB result in \"scrape this game\" now opens an art\nchooser when the game has several images of a wanted kind: a step per\nkind (cover, logo, hero), each a grid of up to 12 images in the order a\nscrape takes them, with \"Keep this one\" first when the game has a file.\nThe chosen image is downloaded in full and replaces the game's file of\nthat kind (as the user's own image does), then the game is scraped.\n\n- Core: IScraper.ArtOptionsAsync, SteamGridDbScraper.ArtOptions (Parse\n  takes the first of each), ScrapeService.GetArtChoicesAsync,\n  GetArtThumbAsync and ScrapeGameWithMatchAsync with chosen images,\n  UserArtService.SetAsync from bytes.\n- App: GameArtPanel, GameMatchPanel opens it, Thumbnails.FromBytes,\n  --open=art for captures.\n- Docs: ARCHITECTURE A2 and decisions log, ROADMAP, manual tests,\n  CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
