+          "date": "2026-10-11T23:04:20Z"
+        },
+        "message": "Game videos on game templates, and a 1990s CRT television\n\nA game template can now play the focused game's own video, with its\nsound, on one of its slot faces: [templates.<id>] video names the slot\nand video_delay_ms (default 1000) how long the game is focused first.\nThe video fades in over the slot's art, loops, and stops when the focus\nmoves, the game launches, the grid hides or the UI layer opens.\n\nEvery game drawn with a template shares its material, so a card video's\ntexture swap would show on all of them. The item shader instead gets a\nvideo_frame sampler and a video_state (cell, slot, aspect, fade) per\nmaterial, so only the focused cell's face shows it and the template\nstays batched, with no new variant. Playback goes through the details\nscreen's VideoPlayback; games' videos are only read when a template the\ntheme uses plays them.\n\nMemory Card gets crt_tv_90s (Tools/CrtTvBuilder: 782 triangles, two\nmaterials), its screen the screenshot slot fitted whole, playing the\nvideo after a second. It's assigned to no system.\n\nBenches (docs/perf/game-videos.md): frame times unchanged; while a\n640x480 video plays, render CPU +0.17 ms, working set +53 MB, video\nmemory +3 MB; on a system without the TV, before and after match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
