+<p class="lead">Features, fixes and companion workflows found across PS2 loaders, forks and tools, together with implemented work, historic proposals and design alternatives. Original entries were source-compared at the date recorded for each audit; <b>subsequent merges can change whether a gap remains open. The October 21 reconciliation and single list above the historical sections supersede older status wording.</b> Project links and evidence are preserved for reproducibility.</p>
+
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">A tracking list, not a roadmap</div>
+An entry documents a source-specific capability absent from RiptOPL or its PS2-Servers companion, with optional design choices and experimental features separately labelled. An entry does not promise a port.
+Broad source comparison dated <b>2026-10-08 UTC</b> (2026-10-07 Pacific); RA merge reconciled on <b>2026-10-08 Pacific</b> against
+<a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/commit/9ef8d643a739d88a4f4b5fd055a209d0b27299c4"><code>rebuild/main@9ef8d643</code></a>.
+This pass rechecks changed OPHTML, LUNA, xeRAbora/OPL-RA and PS2-Launcher sources, verifies the surveyed repositories' current revisions,
+and reconciles already implemented RiptOPL features. Existing historical rows retain their original evidence unless explicitly updated.
+See <a href="#audit-revisions">revision and validation scope</a> and <a href="#notes">retired IDs</a>.
+The October 21 sweep supersedes earlier status statements; see the dated findings and consolidated list. The October 15 supplement added PS2CF and other derivatives. The October 19 focused pass updates shipped states and checks LUNA, PSXCore, PADEMU and PC tools. The broad October 8 baseline is otherwise preserved. <a href="#pc-card-cf">New sections begin at PS2CF</a>. Stable IDs are never reassigned. Tools and developer APIs are distinguished from game-loading features; source, emulator and console evidence are separate.
+</div>
