+<h2 id="ophtml">OPHTML</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML">coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML</a> by <a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions">coffeedevsolutions</a> (Blake Coffee) &mdash; an HTML/CSS declarative UI compiler and zero-allocation C99 GS runtime (<code>OPHTML / ps2ui</code>), by the creator of <a href="#oplattice">OPLattice</a>. While the repository also contains a standalone game launcher (<code>console/ophtml.elf</code>) booting ISOs via Neutrino and an SD2PSX memory-card loader (<code>channel6</code>), those launcher features overlap capabilities already native to RiptOPL (see callout below). Audited against <a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/commit/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1"><code>main@03a5d56</code></a> (post-v0.10.0 source, format v7). The latest published release remains v0.10.0; the reusable console core, settings resolver and memory-card state changes are source additions planned for 0.11.0.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>OH1</code></td><td><b>Declarative HTML/CSS flexbox compilation to zero-allocation C99 GS command list</b></td><td>Compiles modern CSS flexbox layouts (direction, wrap, alignment, justification, gap, percentage sizing, border radius) and dynamic UTF-8 text slots with multibyte truncation guards on the PC into a static <code>.uib</code> binary command list. The C99 runtime executes inside a pre-computed static arena (~7&ndash;8 KiB for an entire 6-screen app) and never calls <code>malloc</code>, measures text, or lays out elements on the PS2.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/tree/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/layout">@ophtml/layout</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">runtime/ps2ui.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH2</code></td><td><b>Pre-resolved pairwise HarfBuzz font kerning on EE</b></td><td>Measures kerning pairs at compile time via HarfBuzz and pre-resolves pairwise advance adjustments to exact pixel values per font size into compact tables. The C99 pen evaluates pairwise kerning in real-time on the EE with zero floating-point division or font-scaling overhead.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/baker/ps2ui_bake/fontgen.py">ps2ui_bake/fontgen.py</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">ps2ui.c kerning</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH3</code></td><td><b>Instant 1-byte palette theme switching without VRAM re-upload</b></td><td>Multiple themes (such as light and dark modes) share the same geometry, textures, and fonts in a single blob, differing only by a row in the tint table. Calling <code>ps2ui_theme_set()</code> updates a context pointer instantly with 0 bytes of VRAM transfer, requiring no asset reloading or GS re-initialization.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.h">ps2ui.h</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">ps2ui.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH4</code></td><td><b>Runtime 2D coordinate offsets for motion and expanding layouts</b></td><td><code>ps2ui_offset_set(ctx, dx, dy)</code> offsets all primitive and texture coordinates at render time, allowing smooth programmatic translations, sliding sidebars (such as expanding navigation rails), carousels, and parallax scrolling layers on static baked geometry without re-baking.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">ps2ui.c offset</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/BACKLOG.md">BACKLOG F27</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH5</code></td><td><b>Runtime focus-subtree visibility masking with auto-bypassing navigation</b></td><td>A 256-bit bitmask in <code>ps2ui_visible_set()</code> suppresses rendering of entire focusable subtrees (including backgrounds and borders) for empty or inactive elements. Crucially, <code>ps2ui_move()</code> automatically routes gamepad focus <i>past</i> hidden nodes rather than trapping navigation on invisible elements.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">ps2ui.c visibility</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/BACKLOG.md">BACKLOG F21</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH6</code></td><td><b>Automated CRT overscan safe area and multi-layer alpha contrast linter</b> <span class="pill">Tool</span></td><td>Build-time static analysis tool enforcing NTSC/PAL CRT action-safe and title-safe margins. Evaluates text contrast across translucent alpha scrims by compositing against worst-case black and white background scenes underneath, and validates seated-distance legibility (11px/14px thresholds based on visual arcminutes).</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/layout/src/lint.js">layout/src/lint.js</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/docs/findings.md">findings.md (F-046)</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH7</code></td><td><b>Interactive web browser theme simulator and testbed</b> <span class="pill">Tool</span></td><td><code>ps2ui serve</code> launches a local HTTP server that replays baked GS draw commands server-side and serves an interactive web preview with keyboard/controller D-pad navigation, theme switching, multi-screen navigation, and live slot text editing without requiring a PS2 console or emulator.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/baker/ps2ui_bake/serve.py">ps2ui_bake/serve.py</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/baker/ps2ui_bake/serve_page.html">serve_page.html</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH8</code></td><td><b>Static VRAM budgeting and layout compiler</b> <span class="pill">Tool</span></td><td>Models GS VRAM allocation at compile time, tracking 8 KiB page boundaries and 256 B block alignment groups for framebuffers, Z-buffers, CLUT palettes, and texture pages. Prevents console crashes and hangs by refusing over-budget themes at bake time with an itemized memory breakdown.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/baker/ps2ui_bake/vram.py">ps2ui_bake/vram.py</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/tools/check-vram-model.py">check-vram-model.py</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH9</code></td><td><b>Headless Play! emulator CI testbed with input scripting and frame diffs</b> <span class="pill">Tool</span></td><td>Continuous integration harness that builds the console ELF, boots it headlessly in the Play! emulator under xvfb, injects scripted gamepad inputs (Down, R1, L1), captures GS framebuffers, and asserts pixel-level image diffs against Python reference renders.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/.github/workflows/hw.yml">.github/workflows/hw.yml</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/console/tests/play_input.py">play_input.py</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH10</code></td><td><b>Fuzzed <code>.uib</code> loader with EE bus-alignment and malformed blob hardening</b> <span class="badge secondary">Fix</span></td><td>Runtime loader hardened with LibFuzzer and ASan/UBSan against corrupted or malicious blobs. Enforces strict 4-byte struct alignment and 16-byte glyph/kern table alignment (<code>PS2UI_ERR_ALIGN</code>) to protect against unaligned EE memory access bus errors when reading untrusted themes from storage.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/tests/fuzz_load.c">fuzz_load.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/runtime/ps2ui.c">ps2ui.c alignment</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>OH11</code></td><td><b>Hard compiler safety limits for untrusted themes</b> <span class="badge secondary">Fix</span></td><td>Compile-time safety ceilings that reject untrusted or maliciously crafted themes exceeding safe hardware parameters: canvas max 2048px (hardware scanout ceiling), max 10,000 DOM elements, max 64 nesting levels, and max 32 megapixel source images.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/baker/ps2ui_bake/caps.py">caps.py</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/packages/layout/src/limits.js">limits.js</a></td></tr>
+      <tr><td><code>OH12</code></td><td><b>Reusable console-launcher core archive</b></td><td>Exports <code>libophtml-console.a</code> and an umbrella header for third-party launchers to reuse scanning, storage initialization, Neutrino argument construction, settings resolution and launch handoff while supplying their own main, UI and IOP module table. RiptOPL has internal equivalents but does not publish this kind of independently linkable launcher SDK. This is a developer integration gap, not additional game compatibility.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/console/ophtml_console.h">Public core header</a><br><a href="https://github.com/coffeedevsolutions/OPHTML/blob/03a5d56f724055f4d46e0eaf44806e95f0202cb1/examples/console-min/Makefile">Out-of-tree consumer</a></td></tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">What did not become a gap: The console launcher &amp; runtime overlap</div>
+OPHTML also contains a standalone console game launcher (<code>console/ophtml.elf</code>) and sample environments (<code>opl-env</code>, <code>channel6</code>), its core game-loading and management capabilities directly overlap existing RiptOPL infrastructure and are not counted as gaps:
+<ul>
+  <li><b>Neutrino No-IOP-Reset launch handoff:</b> OPHTML launches Neutrino using <code>-qb</code>, <code>-bsd=</code>, and <code>-dvd=</code> through <code>LoadELFFromFileWithPartitionNoReset</code>. RiptOPL already has full native No-IOP-Reset handoff (<a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/src/elfldr_noreset.c"><code>src/elfldr_noreset.c</code></a>), copying the child loader into BIOS-unused memory at <code>0x84000</code> and passing target paths and arguments to <code>ExecPS2</code> so Neutrino can read its config and ISO without resetting OPL's live storage mounts.</li>
+  <li><b>In-memory ISO9660 volume &amp; <code>SYSTEM.CNF</code> title ID extraction:</b> OPHTML traverses sector 16 PVD records and parses <code>SYSTEM.CNF</code> in memory. RiptOPL already performs sector 16 PVD root-directory traversal in memory to extract <code>BOOT2</code> game IDs and creation timestamps (<a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/src/retrogem.c"><code>src/retrogem.c</code></a> and <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/src/ps2cnf.c"><code>src/ps2cnf.c</code></a>).</li>
+  <li><b>Dynamic cover art streaming &amp; VRAM texture caching:</b> OPHTML's streaming texture slots overlap RiptOPL's dedicated async texture worker (<a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/src/texcache.c"><code>src/texcache.c</code></a>), which provides lookahead caching, multi-epoch invalidation, chunked staging, memory clamps, and SIO2 controller-bus read throttling.</li>
+  <li><b>Virtualized list windowing &amp; selection binding:</b> OPHTML's <code>ps2ui_list</code> windowing and selection clamping are standard OPL core features in RiptOPL's item and GUI management.</li>
+  <li><b>Multi-device &amp; SD2PSX/MMCE support:</b> USB, internal HDD, MX4SIO, and MMCE channel support are already implemented in RiptOPL's storage drivers and RetroGEM/SD2PSX integration.</li>
+</ul>
+</div>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">Validation status and emulator testing</div>
+OPHTML v0.10.0's <code>ophtml.elf</code> launcher has booted and proven its D-pad navigation and list virtualisation inside the Play! emulator in CI (via automated pad input injection and frame diffing). However, because Play! does not emulate USB, HDD or memory card controllers, physical-console bench cases C1&ndash;C8 remain formally <code>[open]</code> pending physical-console reports. Conversely, its underlying <code>ps2ui</code> GS rasterization runtime has undergone extensive physical PS2 hardware validation across multiple test sessions (documented in <code>docs/bench-phase1.md</code> and <code>docs/bench-phase2.md</code>).
+</div>
+
+<p>The new OPL compatibility resolver maps only verified modes 2, 3 and 5; GSM and VMC CFG mapping remain unfinished. Last-played restoration overlaps RiptOPL. The launch breadcrumb records an attempted handoff but is not a proven hang detector or retry UI; it is not counted as one.</p>
