+    <tr><td><code>T1</code></td><td><b>Graphics patches kept apart from cheats</b></td><td>Graphics patches such as widescreen live in <code>ENH/&lt;id&gt;.enh</code>, separate from gameplay cheats in <code>CHT/</code>. Per-game selections persist independently and graphics patches can carry <code>@auto</code> / <code>@experimental</code> metadata. RiptOPL currently feeds these through its normal cheat path instead of a separate enhancement class.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/TITAN_GAME_PATCHES.md">TITAN_GAME_PATCHES.md</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T2</code></td><td><b>Installable TPKG apps, in-process runtime and SDK</b></td><td>TPKG v2 can install native R5900 application modules that execute inside Titan's application runtime and consume shared UI, input, notification, storage and media services. A public App/Game SDK lets software target Titan itself rather than only launching a separate ELF.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition#product-components">README</a><br><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/TITAN_PACKAGE_FORMAT.md">TPKG format</a><br><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/reference/TITAN_STANDALONE_SDK.md">SDK</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T3</code></td><td><b>Smart IGR overlay with Resume / Return</b> <span class="badge primary">Hardware pending</span></td><td>For titles with a safe compatibility profile, Titan can suspend the running title, show a small in-game overlay, then resume the same threads without ResetEE/GS/IOP or return through the engine cleanup path. Unknown titles fail closed to return-only/legacy behavior. RiptOPL's IGR returns out of the game; it has no equivalent resumable in-game overlay.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/history/imported-root-artifacts/TITAN_SMART_IGR.md">TITAN_SMART_IGR.md</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T4</code></td><td><b>Named user profiles with per-profile VMC</b></td><td>Up to four named users can be created, selected and renamed, each carrying its own avatar and VMC path. RiptOPL has per-game VMC configuration but no system-wide user/profile layer that selects an exclusive VMC by user.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/kernel/src/services/titan_user_profile.h">titan_user_profile.h</a><br><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/kernel/src/services/titan_profile_storage.c">titan_profile_storage.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T5</code></td><td><b>Notification center and background-progress UI</b></td><td>A system Notifications page and top status/ticker surface alerts plus background activity and download progress, including transfer bytes, percentage and speed. RiptOPL has transient dialogs/status text but no comparable system notification/activity service.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/kernel/src/ui/titan_notifications.h">titan_notifications.h</a><br><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/kernel/src/ui/titan_shell_catalog.c">titan_shell_catalog.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T6</code></td><td><b>Integrated lightweight web browser</b></td><td>An installed system app stays inside the running shell and provides URL entry, lightweight HTML text/link parsing, scrolling and back/forward history. HTTP uses PS2IP directly; HTTPS is translated through Titan's configurable Stream Bridge. RiptOPL has network game protocols but no interactive web browser.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/apps/internet-browser/README.md">Internet / Titan Browser</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T7</code></td><td><b>Transactional <code>.pup</code> system updater</b></td><td>Settings can discover forward-only TPUP update packages, verify table/payload CRCs, stage files privately and roll back already-published files if a multi-file update fails. RiptOPL updates are distributed as release artifacts rather than installed by an in-console transactional updater.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/SYSTEM_UPDATE_PUP.md">SYSTEM_UPDATE_PUP.md</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T8</code></td><td><b>Installable animated scene themes with audio</b></td><td><code>.tthm</code> packages can provide full HOME/TOP scene frames, reversible transition keyframes, bounded idle loops, background music, navigation/interface sounds and icon styling. RiptOPL's theme engine does not have Titan's packaged state/keyframe scene-animation model.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/THEME_AUTHORING.md">THEME_AUTHORING.md</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T9</code></td><td><b>Xbox Bluetooth/BLE plus USB keyboard and mouse input</b> <span class="badge primary">Hardware pending</span></td><td>Titan's Unified Input has source paths for Bluetooth-capable Xbox One and Xbox Series pads over Bluetooth/BLE, plus USB keyboard and mouse input. Wired Xbox USB is already counted as <a href="#ps2-launcher">P1</a>; this row counts Titan's additional Bluetooth/HID input classes. Titan explicitly labels these host-contract PASS but physical-PS2 validation pending.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/history/imported-root-artifacts/TITAN_MODERN_CONTROLLER_MATRIX.md">Modern Controller Matrix</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>T10</code></td><td><b>Repository-backed package download pipeline</b> <span class="badge primary">Target pending</span></td><td>Titan can accept a static repository catalog, resolve package/dependency metadata, queue HTTP/HTTPS package downloads, verify size and SHA-256 plus TPKG structure, then atomically publish the package for installation. Its documentation calls this a Store foundation rather than a finished storefront and says real target downloads remain pending.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/TITAN_STORE_ARCHITECTURE.md">Store architecture</a><br><a href="https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/blob/main/docs/TITAN_DOWNLOAD_SERVICE.md">Download Service</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">Titan validation and overlap notes</div>
+Titan distinguishes source/host-contract completion from physical-PS2 validation. In particular, Smart IGR, the modern-controller paths and Store/Download path are kept above because this page audits implemented code capabilities, but Titan's own hardware/target-pending labels are preserved rather than treating them as proven compatibility.<br><br>
+Several other Titan capabilities are real but do not get extra T-series IDs because the same RiptOPL gap is already represented elsewhere on this page: direct cover/background fetching overlaps <a href="#ps2-launcher">P2</a>, its native wLaunchELF work overlaps <a href="#boliviaos">B1</a>, Project NES overlaps <a href="#retrolauncher">R1</a>, its launch transition overlaps <a href="#ps2-launcher">P5</a>, and wired Xbox USB overlaps <a href="#ps2-launcher">P1</a>. Titan's Neutrino/UL launching, VMC support and ordinary PS2RD cheats also have RiptOPL equivalents and are not gaps by themselves.
+</div>
