+<h2 id="nhddl">NHDDL</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/pcm720/nhddl">pcm720/nhddl</a> &mdash; a deliberately small Neutrino front-end whose
+README explicitly keeps OPL-only features such as PADEMU, IGR and cheats out of scope unless Neutrino itself provides
+them. Audited against the released <a href="https://github.com/pcm720/nhddl/tree/v1.2.2">v1.2.2</a> code and documentation.
+The core features most likely to look unique at first glance are already present in RiptOPL: PixelFX/RetroGEM visual
+Game ID signalling, per-title SD2PSX/MemCard PRO2 card switching, cover art, persistent title caching, remembered
+last-played selection, global and per-game Neutrino arguments, VMC handoff and the principal Neutrino storage backends.
+The two remaining differences below are launcher/network conveniences rather than missing game-source support.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>N1</code></td><td><b>Generic forward-boot CLI</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>Launching NHDDL with <code>-mode=&lt;type&gt;</code> and <code>-dvd=&lt;path&gt;</code> bypasses its UI and hands the target straight to Neutrino; <code>-noinit</code> can reuse an environment whose modules are already loaded. RiptOPL has positional HDD/BDM autolaunch entry points, but not an equivalent documented generic backend/path command line.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/pcm720/nhddl/blob/v1.2.2/README.md#forward-boot-mode">Forward Boot Mode</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>N2</code></td><td><b>Reuse <code>SYS-CONF/IPCONFIG.DAT</code> for UDPFS IP</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>When no explicit <code>udpfs_ip</code> is supplied, NHDDL can obtain the PS2 network address from the wLaunchELF/uLaunchELF-style <code>SYS-CONF/IPCONFIG.DAT</code>. RiptOPL's <a href="network-boot.html">UDPFS</a> path currently uses its own Network settings and the active Neutrino TOML instead of inheriting that shared file.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/pcm720/nhddl/blob/v1.2.2/README.md#udpfs">UDPFS documentation</a><br><a href="https://github.com/pcm720/nhddl/commit/81905e1f68f50ded828fe59a04f6313a9c4f21de">IPCONFIG.DAT fix</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">What did not become a gap</div>
+NHDDL's visual Game ID output and SD2PSX/MemCard PRO2 per-title switching both have direct RiptOPL equivalents.
+RiptOPL also already remembers the last-played title, caches parsed ISO metadata, supports global and per-game Neutrino
+arguments, and can hand VMCs to Neutrino. NHDDL's backend-forcing ELF filename suffixes are a different configuration
+interface for selecting a device mode, not a separate game-loading capability, so they are not counted independently.
+</div>
