+<h2 id="luna">LUNA</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA">LUNA</a> by <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx">darkladark</a> is a visual NHDDL/Neutrino-derived loader.
+Earlier comparison: <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/commit/475f7b2513e739cf63af9cd4ed8c84280e93a762"><code>475f7b25</code></a>,
+pinning frontend <code>e9554ce6</code> and runtime <code>02cbf4f2</code>. These are separate repositories; implementation links below point to their exact gitlink revisions.
+The current views are List, Collections, 3D, Orbit and experimental Scroll. Constellation (LU1) and the old flat Grid (LU3) are historical, not current capabilities.</p>
+<p><b>Collection display overlap:</b> <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/977">RiptOPL #977</a> adapts the Collection display from #733 as the native <a href="coverflow.html#psbbn-flow">PSBBN Flow</a> theme. It preserves R3 Favorites and uses the existing menu and artwork cache. This perspective fan does not implement LUNA's orbital ring or projected 3D grid listed below.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>LU2</code></td><td><b>Orbit depth-sorted ring library view</b></td><td>Renders the selected game at the front of a tilted ring while the other cached covers move around it with perspective narrowing, size/brightness/opacity depth falloff and explicit rear-to-front sorting. RiptOPL's Coverflow is a linear carousel and has no equivalent orbital presentation.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/ui/view_orbit.c">view_orbit.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU4</code></td><td><b>Animated rotating <code>ICO</code> disc-label artwork</b></td><td>Classic view pairs the normal OPL <code>_COV.png</code> with <code>_ICO.png</code> disc art and rotates the disc texture continuously on a textured quad. RiptOPL already understands <code>ICO</code> as disc artwork and can toggle it at runtime, so the gap is specifically the animated disc presentation, not disc-art support itself.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/ui/view_classic.c">view_classic.c</a><br>paired-art behavior is evidenced by the pinned implementation linked above</td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU5</code></td><td><b>Per-drive Favorites that travel with the game HDD</b> <span class="pill">Optional</span></td><td>LUNA resolves Favorites against the selected title's metadata device and stores them under that drive's <code>/LUNA/favorites.txt</code>; swapping game HDDs therefore swaps the Favorites set with the library. RiptOPL deliberately keeps one cross-device <code>favourites.bin</code> beside its shared master configuration, so this is a different persistence model rather than missing Favorites functionality.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/favorites.c">favorites.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/src/favsupport.c">RiptOPL favsupport.c</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU6</code></td><td><b>Staged temp-file writes for key persistent library state</b> <span class="badge secondary">Fix</span></td><td>LUNA writes a complete temporary file before replacing <code>favorites.txt</code>, <code>lastTitle.bin</code> and the ISO title-ID <code>cache.bin</code>; readers can recover completed temporary last-title/cache records after interrupted replacement. <b>2026-10-15: partial parity.</b> RiptOPL now first writes <code>favourites.bin.new</code>, retains that complete copy across an interrupted main-file rewrite, and recovers it on load (<a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pull/945">PR #945</a>). It still cannot use an atomic rename on every memory-card filesystem; LUNA's separate last-title/cache staging details warrant independent comparison.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/favorites.c">Favorites staging</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/options.c">last-title staging</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/devices/iso.c">cache staging</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU7</code></td><td><b>Neutrino physical power-button DEV9-safe shutdown</b> <span class="badge secondary">Fix</span></td><td>LUNA modifies Neutrino's IOP CD/DVD service so the native front-panel power event is handled by a priority-1 listener: it stops/synchronizes active emulated optical work, invokes DEV9's shutdown export when present, then issues the normal <code>sceCdPowerOff</code>. RiptOPL's OPL core already has its own orderly IGR/power-off path, but its <b>Neutrino</b> core does not include this coordinated DEV9 shutdown behavior.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/iop/cdvdfsv/src/cdvdfsv.c">LUNA cdvdfsv.c</a><br><a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/neutrino/blob/master/iop/cdvdfsv/src/cdvdfsv.c">RiptOPL Neutrino baseline</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU8</code></td><td><b>Neutrino in-game return / IGR</b></td><td>LUNA extends the <b>Neutrino</b> runtime itself with a held <code>L1+L2+R1+R2+START+SELECT</code> IGR path. After 45 VBlank frames (roughly one second) it calls LUNA's shutdown RPC to quiesce optical/DEV9 activity, then uses the configured <code>eec.ExitPath</code> as the return ELF path, resets IOP and EE/GS state, and uses <code>ExecPS2()</code> to return directly to the memory-card ELF. RiptOPL has OPL-side IGR, but games launched through its current Neutrino core do <b>not</b> have Neutrino IGR, so this is a distinct missing runtime capability. The current README reports a physical FAT-PS2 test and requires installation on a memory card; this remains narrower than validation across all console and storage combinations.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/ee/ee_core/src/padhook.c">pad hook / combo</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/ee/ee_core/src/luna_igr_rpc.c">EE IGR RPC client</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/iop/cdvdfsv/src/cdvdfsv.c">IOP shutdown RPC</a><br><a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/docs/IGR.md">RiptOPL IGR scope</a></td></tr>
