+    <tr><td><code>LU10</code></td><td><b>Animated ambient-orb Scroll library view</b></td><td>An explicitly experimental library presentation pairing scrolling title/logo artwork with animated ambient orbs. RiptOPL has animated backgrounds and title lists, but no corresponding selectable orb/scroll library view. The comparison concerns the complete browsing presentation, not generic animation support.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/ui/view_scroll.c">Scroll renderer</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/nhddl-luna/blob/e9554ce6affa133fd776a7e1265580608832821e/src/ui/gui.c">Scroll navigation</a></td></tr>
+    <tr><td><code>LU11</code></td><td><b>Neutrino VMC backing on APA/PFS</b></td><td>Maps raw VMC files from an APA/PFS metadata partition into direct ATA extents for the Neutrino runtime. Requires normal boot, 8 KiB PFS zones, no indirect inode segments, and a shared 64-fragment budget for game plus both cards. The loader validates image geometry and mapping before launch. RiptOPL currently drops Neutrino VMC arguments for APA games because its bundled runtime lacks this PFS backing path. LUNA still requests a physical-console save/reboot/reload test; source implementation does not establish broad game compatibility.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/ee/loader/src/pfs_vmc.c">PFS extent mapping</a><br><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/neutrino-luna/blob/02cbf4f2a0bafcba71904f7d9d8fcda6ddd65f15/ee/loader/src/main.c">Loader restrictions</a><br><a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/9ef8d643a739d88a4f4b5fd055a209d0b27299c4/docs/NEUTRINO.md">RiptOPL APA VMC restriction</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>LU15</code></td><td><b>Native PS1 in-game return menu</b></td><td>LUNA builds PSXCore with <code>NP_IGR_RETURN=1</code> to show a native Quit/Play overlay and attempt a memory-card ELF return. RiptOPL's PS1 paths do not provide the same integrated Quit/Return panel: Ember lacks IGR; POPStarter has its own reset behavior. Finishing a save before return remains the user's responsibility, and physical-console save safety is not established.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/blob/4614b0c53e0f904a57afb18572b15090a6afd657/tools/build-luna-psxcore.sh">LUNA build configuration</a> · <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore/blob/360a788ff7bb7c6853702a8edec6860cae49c0a2/runtime/igrloader/main.c">return routine</a> · <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/docs/VCD.md">RiptOPL PS1 limitations</a></td></tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">Current overlap and validation scope</div>
+Storage-source toggles, rescans, card creation/assignment, optional music and cheat selection are not counted again: RiptOPL already has those categories of functionality.
+LUNA's current README reports in-game return on a physical FAT PS2, while APA/PFS VMC save/reboot/reload and artwork performance on optional storage still need console testing.
+The older Constellation/Grid descriptions and HDD-only filter are superseded by the current frontend; neither describes today's selectable library views.
