+<h2 id="sopl">Stable Open PS2 Loader (sOPL)</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/mystyq/Stable-Open-PS2-Loader">mystyq/Stable-Open-PS2-Loader</a> &mdash; a
+stability-focused fork. Its artwork TAR caching, large-list work, BDM HDD support, game-size fixes, MMCE work and
+other older changes either exist in RiptOPL or have since been superseded there. One lower-level ATA behavior remains
+materially different.</p>
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>What it does</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td><code>S1</code></td><td><b>ATA DRDY waiting for slow-starting SMR / SSD drives</b> <span class="badge secondary">Fix</span></td><td>sOPL's in-game ATAD path adds an <code>ata_wait_until_ready()</code> loop that waits for BUSY to clear and DRDY to assert at driver start and around ATA commands. It was introduced specifically for newer SMR/SSD drives that can take longer to become ready. RiptOPL has its own post-ATAD settling and HDD-detection safeguards, but its current <code>cdvdman/atad.c</code> does not implement this in-driver DRDY wait strategy.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/mystyq/Stable-Open-PS2-Loader/commit/3495d55b96ce72497b6a922ab540ac76a58ca74a">commit 3495d55b</a><br><a href="https://github.com/mystyq/Stable-Open-PS2-Loader/blob/master/modules/iopcore/cdvdman/atad.c">current atad.c</a></td></tr>
+  </tbody>
+</table>
+<div class="callout info"><div class="h">sOPL TAR claims vs. audited source</div>
+The May 2026 sOPL release text advertises <code>ART/art.tar</code>, <code>CFG/cfg.tar</code> and <code>CHT/cht.tar</code>.
+The published <code>release</code> tag points to an older commit, while current <code>master</code> visibly carries the
+ART reader/cache path. This survey does not turn an unlocated release-note claim into a separate gap. More importantly,
+RiptOPL <code>rebuild/main</code> now has a unified TAR engine for all three archive kinds, including
+<code>art_cache.bin</code>, <code>cfg_cache.bin</code> and <code>cht_cache.bin</code>, so none of those archive features
+is a current RiptOPL gap regardless.
+</div>
