+</tbody></table>
+<p><b>Audited code:</b> The <a href="https://github.com/Rian6/caduceus-opl/tree/2a98a9d7361f8e33f421244bc88c318eab3bdf2f">actual OPL snapshot</a> was compared against <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/tree/7452341a076d3e7a5e14e613429c7eca594f4888">RiptOPL code</a>, and the <a href="https://github.com/Rian6/caduceus/tree/311f4eabc4ddaad649cbd0d60859f27d0ffcbbfc">Caduceus desktop modules</a> against <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/PS2-Servers/tree/c1eb1e5aecd9e8359dc5b7799fc7f135a81f51d5">PS2-Servers</a>. RiptOPL already has normal RA hashing, watch lists, SMB reconnect, PNG artwork support and an in-game unlock indicator; none is newly counted as missing. CO4 is richer presentation, not a missing RA notification system. CO6 is a more proactive check, not missing basic SMB recovery. Caduceus OPL's custom account protocol needs a companion endpoint and cannot be obtained just by swapping SMB servers.</p>
+
+<p><a href="https://github.com/Rian6/caduceus">Rian6/Caduceus</a> is the Windows-side application (Electron/React/TypeScript/SQLite) that manages a game catalogue and launches the separately sourced <a href="https://github.com/elmariolo/OPL-Server">OPLServer</a> SMB server. <a href="https://github.com/Rian6/caduceus-opl">Rian6/Caduceus OPL</a> is its cooperating console-side OPL derivative. That is a <b>tightly paired host + console loader</b>, not one interchangeable executable. Their source repositories are distinct; the OPL source is also tracked as an <code>opl-snapshot</code> submodule.</p>
+<p>Our comparable pairing is <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/PS2-Servers">PS2-Servers</a> (host-side network service) and <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader">RiptOPL</a> (PS2 launcher). PS2-Servers deliberately serves multiple kinds of PS2 clients; Caduceus invests more heavily in a companion library and account experience. The table identifies <b>host-side product gaps</b> as well as console-side differences, without treating them as interchangeable RiptOPL feature gaps.</p>
