+<h2 id="ripps2">RIPPS2 — RiptOPL-derived integrated launcher (October 2026)</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2">akilluminati47/RIPPS2</a> is an actively developed, PS2-native derivative of RiptOPL. Its October beta publishes build-specific patch source and host tests. The entries below focus on <em>functionally differentiated</em> tools and interaction models; its ordinary OPL game loading, carousel and fetched cover art overlap capabilities already counted here (e.g. B1, P2/P3, CO3 and OR4), and should not create duplicate generic IDs.</p>
+<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Feature</th><th>Gap and boundaries</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td><code>RI1</code></td><td><b>Browse VMCs as folders; import/export PSU saves</b></td><td>Integrated <em>Memory Files</em> browser treats virtual memory-card images as navigable save containers, with file copy/move and PSU import/export. Beyond the generic file-explorer concept already tracked as B1. Importing into VMCs must be transactional, guarded and backup-first before RiptOPL parity is claimed.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/main/elf/patches/0098-ripps2-build98-memory-files.patch">Memory Files patch</a> · <a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/main/README.md">features</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>RI2</code></td><td><b>Physical memory-card manager</b> <span class="pill">High-risk</span></td><td>Dedicated backup to VMC, restore saves and card erase/format workflow from the launcher. These are <b>optional, potentially destructive</b> operations: RiptOPL must not silently change cards or introduce formatting without explicit confirmation, backup and restore tests.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/main/elf/patches/0086-ripps2-build86-card-manager-neutrino-logo-first.patch">card manager patch</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>RI3</code></td><td><b>Paused in-game actions panel</b> <span class="badge primary">Experimental</span></td><td>Overlay provides Resume, Achievements and Exit Game from an IGR combination. Distinct from RiptOPL's existing achievement notifications and OPL IGR; related in broad concept to the previously tracked Neutrino/ORBIT in-game UI. RIPPS2 itself leaves the menu disabled by default pending stronger console evidence: never call this hardware-proven across video modes.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/main/elf/patches/0087-ripps2-build87-in-game-menu.patch">IGR menu patch</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>RI4</code></td><td><b>Offline personal BIOS audio / theme-pack tool</b> <span class="pill">Tool</span></td><td>The PC-side Audio Studio converts user-supplied audio (and locally provided BIOS assets) to ADP/OGG theme packs. This is a separate optional authoring workflow, not a reason to redistribute BIOS audio or copyrighted system assets.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/tree/main/tools/audio-studio">audio-studio</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td><code>RI5</code></td><td><b>Stable keyed language packs and layered glyph fallback</b> (Build 104, source available but beta not yet released)</td><td>RIPPS2's <code>#!RIPPS2LANG 1</code> translation files address strings by the FNV-1a hash of English text instead of the line ordinal. Missing/new strings fall back to English, malformed printf placeholders are rejected, older position-indexed packs remain readable, and non-ASCII/CJK glyph fallback uses per-language fonts. RiptOPL already supports 30+ translated UI languages, UTF-8 and an optional CJK game-title fallback, but <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/docs/LANGUAGES.md">its external language packs use append-only positional IDs</a>. This is specifically a version-tolerance, malformed-translation safety and font-layout gap, <b>not</b> a claim RiptOPL lacks translations. RIPPS2 still documents missing Arabic/Persian shaping and Lao font coverage.</td><td><a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/e8f317b2196f625ae1947f3d1aeae547d232ee62/CHANGELOG.md">Build 104 changelog</a> · <a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/e8f317b2196f625ae1947f3d1aeae547d232ee62/elf/lang/ripps2lang.py">language pack generator</a> · <a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/blob/e8f317b2196f625ae1947f3d1aeae547d232ee62/docs/plans/builds-104-on.md">implementation/test notes</a></td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<p><b>October 19 source/release distinction:</b> <a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/commit/e8f317b2196f625ae1947f3d1aeae547d232ee62">RIPPS2 main@e8f317b</a> contains Build 104 language work, but the latest published beta checked was <a href="https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/releases/tag/v1.0.2-beta">v1.0.2 (Build 102)</a>. Build 105's disc-to-storage ripping, Build 106's in-game screenshots and Build 107's file-search are <em>plans</em>, not demonstrated features, so they are <b>not</b> registered as gaps. Build 103's import of newer RiptOPL source is likewise not a missing feature in RiptOPL itself.</p>
