+<h3 id="udpfs-server-batch">Network-server ecosystem checked without new source-specific gaps</h3>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/pcm720/udpfsd">pcm720/udpfsd</a> supports isolated concurrent UDPFS clients, read-only mode, UDPBD-with-UDPFS transport, Go binaries for embedded targets and optional CGO/libchdr CHD handling. <a href="https://github.com/YouKnow-sys/udpfs-server">YouKnow-sys/udpfs-server</a> packages this family for Android. <a href="https://github.com/GorGylka/Server2PS2">GorGylka/Server2PS2</a> provides an embedded Luckfox/Pico hardware deployment with SMB/UDPBD/UDPFS and a physical BOOT-button/LED mode selector. RiptOPL's <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/PS2-Servers/blob/main/docs/EDITIONS.md">PS2-Servers Desktop/Core/Edge</a> already has UDPFS, UDPBD, SMB, embedded web UI, multi-client modes and portable deployment. None of those protocol categories is a newly missing RiptOPL game source; a device-specific button-controlled appliance is a different packaging/hardware proposition. Track as integration and server-protocol regression references rather than inflating feature counts. <b>Edge does not presently include CHD or SMB2/3</b>; Desktop/Core retain CHD where libchdr is installed. No end-to-end comparison on actual PS2 hardware was performed in this audit.</p>
+<p><b>Audit boundary:</b> this batch compared selected source modules, declarations, documentation and previous fork-gap evidence. The new entries are recorded as <em>source-verified differences</em> with explicit compatibility caveats. Other pre-existing IDs remain subject to the separate full re-audit described <a href="#audit-method">below</a>.</p>
+
