+<h3>PSXCore (PX1–PX10) &mdash; POPStarter and Ember parity</h3>
+<p><b>Pinned revisions:</b> <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/commit/4614b0c53e0f904a57afb18572b15090a6afd657">LUNA@4614b0c5</a> still pins <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore/tree/360a788ff7bb7c6853702a8edec6860cae49c0a2">PSXCore@360a788f</a>. Public PSXCore moved one commit to <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore/commit/66c70e9f920c39ebbe8c3d1deb7cfc7a78cf4fc9">66c70e9f</a> (bounded unaligned upload-copy code), <em>not</em> yet integrated into LUNA. Since the last fork-gap PR update, LUNA itself changed README text only; this section audits features previously underclassified from its October 17–19 work.</p>
+<p><b>Do not confuse runtime architectures.</b> <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/blob/rebuild/main/docs/VCD.md">RiptOPL already launches PS1 VCDs via POPStarter</a>, which uses Sony POPS. <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore">PSXCore</a> likewise adapts the user-supplied Sony POPS executable in memory; it is not an independent emulator. <a href="https://github.com/Gageformer/Ember/blob/main/README.md">Ember</a> implements its own PS1 emulation from CUE/BIN data. Internal POPS patches cannot be transferred blindly to Ember, and without matched game/hardware tests a different source implementation is not proof of better compatibility.</p>
