+<h4>Experimental and incomplete capabilities (also inventoried)</h4>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore/blob/66c70e9f920c39ebbe8c3d1deb7cfc7a78cf4fc9/DISC-MAPPING.md">Prepared native APA/PFS mapping</a> is an experimental API and does not make an APA game browser/loader; RiptOPL's current POPStarter already has APA support. The <a href="https://github.com/dnunezx/PSXCore/blob/66c70e9f920c39ebbe8c3d1deb7cfc7a78cf4fc9/src/compat_profiles.generated.h">published automatic compatibility profile catalog has zero entries</a>. Adaptive Audio is OFF by default in the tester and may affect tempo/pitch. MX4SIO/MMCE and multiple USB support are not proven in the standalone tester. PSXCore's tester release has <b>no established physical-console gameplay or save/reload validation</b>, and IGR/disc swapping are disabled there, despite LUNA's separately configured runtime.</p>
+<h4>Validation and safe implementation scope</h4>
+<p>Preserve POPStarter and Ember as default choices. Any experimental PSXCore integration must verify user-provided POPS file checksums, patch bytes, ELF layout, per-title storage and memory-card ownership before IOP handoff. Compare identical legal disc data across all <em>supported</em> runtimes for startup, GPU/GTE effects, MDEC/FMVs, SPU/reverb/CDDA, controller behavior, disc swap, native saves after full reboot and IGR return. Label source presence, host-test success and actual hardware outcomes independently. No automatic migration, overwritten memory cards, blanket POPS patches, exclusive device claims or premature release.</p>
+<h3>OPL-DS4RTBT (DT1–DT3)</h3>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/MiguelQueiroz010/OPL-DS4RTBT/tree/rtl-fw-loader">RTL-enabled Bluetooth fork</a> adds Realtek firmware handling (DT1), DS4 clone HID output/CRC and rumble (DT2), and four-pad menu status plus controller setup/test (DT3). These extend <a href="#dualsense-bt">DB1–DB2</a> (original DualSense BT/pairing), and are fully scoped in <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/issues/972">issue #972</a>. Distinguish four <em>menu</em> pads from in-game multitap. Firmware licensing and real hardware remain verification gates.</p>
+<h3>PS2 Manager for macOS (MA1–MA2)</h3>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/Gionnio/ps2manager">Native macOS manager</a> supports PS2 ISO imports and PS1 CUE/BIN-to-VCD conversion with POPStarter multi-disc package sidecars (MA1), and per-game user-supplied POPS patch archives plus VCD reverse conversion (MA2). These are desktop-library workflow candidates for PS2-Servers and external utilities rather than missing OPL game-core functions.</p>
+</section>
+
+<h2 id="audit-method">Audit methodology and project coverage</h2>
+<p>“Fork gap” is a source-specific difference, <b>not</b> an invitation to copy every fork, or a guarantee that a feature works on every PS2. Each record should establish: (1) a named upstream revision or release; (2) a relevant implementation file or tested feature; (3) the corresponding RiptOPL behavior on a named branch; (4) whether the difference is an actual missing function, an optional design, a companion capability, an experimental claim, or already implemented; and (5) the evidence level: source / host tests / PCSX2 / real console.</p>
+<p><b>Inclusive recording policy:</b> Existing parity, UI alternatives, companion features, experimental flags, unsupported cases, bugs, withdrawn/historical work, and proposals remain documented and classified. Branding-only or empty forks can remain as directory references; they are not misrepresented as implemented code. Multiple sources may refer to one capability, and the record total is not a count of missing features. Mark delivered work as implemented instead of deleting it.</p>
+<p><b>Reporting another project:</b> link its repository or official source, exact branch/commit, feature code and hardware validation, then show where RiptOPL lacks (or already contains) it. Before creating another gap ID, check the <a href="#at-a-glance">register</a>, the <a href="#project-directory">A–Z directory</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/pulls">active PRs</a>. Source differences affecting Launchstation, POPSLoader, launcHER or PS2-Servers should identify that companion rather than incorrectly claim an OPL game-loader gap.</p>
+<p><b>Freshness:</b> the October 8 comprehensive baseline has not been re-executed end-to-end. The October 15 pass corrects the five explicitly demonstrated implemented records, documents one partial-parity case and one closed historical proposal, and expands the project directory. The remaining records require revision-specific rechecks; their presence is not an assertion that they remain absent at HEAD.</p>
+</section>
