+    {
+      "repo": "dnunezx/LUNA",
+      "release": {
+        "tag": "v3.1.3",
+        "published": "2026-10-19T12:43:24Z",
+        "url": "https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/releases/tag/v3.1.3",
+        "body": "![LUNA 3.1.3 demonstration](https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/blob/35c7183427913005d58bdb9433ccf6420a9d6167/LUNA-3.1.3-demo.gif?raw=true)\r\n\r\n**Starting-disc selection and native in-game disc swapping is fully functional**\r\n\r\n>  PSXCore is now the most compatible PS1 emulator available for PS2. Please report any issues you encounter. \r\n\r\n## Changes since LUNA 2.0.0 Stable\r\n\r\n### PlayStation games, disc swapping, and in-game return\r\n\r\n- Added **PSXCore** integration: discover and launch PS1 VCD games from internal ATA and USB storage alongside PS2 games.\r\n- Added the **L3 platform filter** for Mix, PS2, and PS1 libraries, with saved selection and a brief mode-change notification.\r\n- Added **two-to-four-disc sets** grouped into one library entry. Create, edit, reorder, and remove sets in LUNA, or supply an `.m3u` playlist. Nearby disc-name matches can be offered as suggestions for confirmation.\r\n- Added saved **starting-disc selection** and native **in-game disc swapping**. Hold **L2 + R2 + Select** with one D-pad direction, then release. The pre-launch screen shows the direction-to-disc mapping for the chosen starting disc.\r\n- Added validation of disc identity, missing or duplicate images, changed content, shared volume identity, and memory-card bindings. Changed images can be explicitly revalidated through disc management.\r\n- Added **PS1 in-game return to LUNA**, using the familiar **L1 + L2 + R1 + R2 + Start + Select** combination to open the native menu. Confirm return to load `mc0:/APP_LUNA/luna.elf`.\r\n- Bundled the latest unchanged upstream **PSXCore `360a788`**, including its new LUNA-styled English return menu. **Disc swapping and in-game return are enabled together in this package.**\r\n- Replaced written button names in the disc-swap prompt with controller icons and directional arrows. Added a dark reading panel, brighter and larger text, larger grouped icons, a readable Select button, and clearer disc rows.\r\n- Added per-game **Code Validation** selection, fixed PS1 file launches on exFAT, and added firmware size/hash checks before leaving the library.\r\n\r\n### Memory cards and save management\r\n\r\n- Added automatic creation of missing **default shared PS1 memory cards**, plus named card pairs and per-game pair selection. Disc sets retain their selected pair across swaps.\r\n- Added a separate **PlayStation card manager** with import, export, paired backups, and recovery of interrupted card operations.\r\n- Connected **PS2 virtual memory-card assignments** to game launches, including the matching OPL runtime and supported APA/PFS mappings.\r\n- Improved card validation, interrupted-operation recovery, settings persistence, and staged-file handling. Existing saves remain on the game drive.\r\n\r\n### PS2 launch engines, compatibility, and cheats\r\n\r\n- Added **OPL as an alternate PS2 launch engine**, selectable globally or per game; Neutrino remains the default. Bundled OPL backends cover ATA/FAT32/exFAT, APA/HDL, USB, MX4SIO, iLink, MMCE, and UDPFS.\r\n- Added engine-specific compatibility and video controls, clearer default-option summaries, and a dedicated game-core section.\r\n- Added **per-game cheat selection** from `CHT/<TITLE_ID>.cht` through the matching Neutrino runtime. This path uses raw PS2RD codes; cheats are off by default.\r\n- Corrected OPL handoff memory layout and HDD addressing, and fixed launch handling of saved global and per-game startup-logo choices.\r\n- Updated the matching Neutrino runtime, virtual-card handling, and in-game return integration.\r\n\r\n### Library views, artwork, and responsiveness\r\n\r\n- Redesigned **Scroll** around a horizontal title-logo strip and cover carousel, with depth, a larger selected cover, neighboring-artwork loading, title-text fallback, and glass-themed missing-cover placeholders.\r\n- Scroll logos use `ART/SCROLL/<TITLE_ID>_LGO.png`. Removed the old per-title wallpaper and game-information panel from Scroll.\r\n- Added **PS1 jewel-case or tall-case styling** in List and 3D, plus configurable Separate or Overlap cover/disc layout in List. View appearance controls now sit together under Views.\r\n- Added **3D page transitions**, softer case thumbnails, and safer artwork uploads while drawing.\r\n- Improved **Collections** entry with seven prepared covers, cached-artwork reuse, and fewer loading interruptions.\r\n- Improved **Orbit** cover reuse and crossfades, reducing flashing placeholders during browsing.\r\n- Optimized artwork caching, thumbnail reuse, visible List rows, game lookup, Favorites updates, and view switching for larger libraries.\r\n- Restored and preserved **stable 2.0 animation and navigation timing** in Collections and Orbit while retaining artwork optimizations.\r\n\r\n### Backgrounds, languages, and menus\r\n\r\n- Added animated backgrounds including **Neo, Aurora, Ronin, Gridrunner, Torch, and Tempest**, with a nighttime Gridrunner scene.\r\n- Added saved **English, Spanish, and Brazilian Portuguese** selection, translated UI text, and UTF-8 support in both fonts.\r\n- Added configurable **Ambient Orbs formations**, including skull and atom shapes, with saved enabled-shape choices.\r\n- Polished the main menu and Options layout, blue selection accents, focus highlights, glass contrast, default-value summaries, and save feedback.\r\n- Improved quick-menu readability and closing behavior, added R1 dismissal, and removed duplicate icon shadows.\r\n- Fixed menu-title alignment, font fading, and overlapping per-game video-mode text.\r\n\r\n### File Explorer and storage\r\n\r\n- Expanded **File Explorer** with storage and memory-card browsing, folder navigation, paging, contextual actions, and clearer button prompts.\r\n- Added a persistent **copy tray**, multi-item marking, copy/move workflows, transfer progress, and **Skip / Keep Both / Replace** choices for name conflicts.\r\n- Added folder creation, rename, deletion, file/folder details, filtering, and sorting by name, size, or date. Moves verify copied data before removing their source.\r\n- Added read-only **text/configuration previews** and direct launching of compatible PS2 homebrew ELF files after confirmation.\r\n- Improved storage rescans, including empty-library recovery and preserving the display during refreshes.\r\n\r\n### Reliability and packaging\r\n\r\n- Fixed hardware-freeze causes involving runtime locks, artwork upload limits, and worker-stack reuse during shutdown.\r\n- Hardened ISO scanning and title-cache validation. Scan and transfer failures preserve previous library state and move sources.\r\n- Improved recovery of staged Favorites saves, configuration writes, graphics-allocation failures, texture lifetimes, and repeated cleanup.\r\n- Bundled matching hardware builds of LUNA, PSXCore, Neutrino, and OPL, with license notices and SHA-256 checksums. Optional music remains a separate add-on.\r\n\r\n## Installation\r\n\r\nDownload **`LUNA-v3.1.3-FMCB-mc0.zip`**, extract it, and copy the complete **`APP_LUNA`** folder to **`mc0:/APP_LUNA`**. \r\n\r\nFor PS1 games, place VCD images and optional `.m3u` playlists under **`/VCD/`** on a HDD or USB drive. Supply your own matching **`/POPS/POPS.ELF`** and **`/POPS/IOPRP252.IMG`**. Firmware, games, and saves are not included,\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\nThe versioned hardware launcher, unchanged PSXCore runtime, Neutrino runtime, and OPL backends built successfully. PSXCore launch-layout validation, package file checks, ZIP contents, and SHA-256 checksums passed.\r\n\r\n[Full source changes since LUNA 2.0.0 Stable](https://github.com/dnunezx/LUNA/compare/v2.0.0...v3.1.3)\r\n"
+      }
