+        "body": "Embers basic frontend launcher to get you started\r\n\r\n- Now supports all devices. Drop it next to ember.elf like before, or utilize the config to choose your directory\r\n- Now can scroll, hold the d-pad instead of manually pressing each iteration\r\n\r\n**Using the config**\r\n\r\nYou only need `ember-launcher.cfg` if the launcher is NOT in the same folder as `ember.elf`. If it is, the file is ignored.\r\n\r\n1. Keep `ember-launcher.cfg` in the same folder as the launcher.\r\n2. Open it in a text editor and remove the `#` from the line for your device. Change the folder name if yours isn't `EMBER`.\r\n3. Start the launcher. Your games are listed from that folder's `games/` as usual.\r\n\r\nCommon lines:\r\n\r\n    ember=mmce?:/EMBER/                  MMCE (SD2PSX, MemCard PRO2)\r\n    ember=mass:/EMBER/                   USB\r\n    ember=mx4sio:/EMBER/                 MX4SIO\r\n    ember=ata:/EMBER/                    Internal HDD, exFAT\r\n    ember=hdd0:<partition>:pfs:/EMBER/   Internal HDD, APA/PFS\r\n\r\nPoint it at the folder that holds `ember.elf`, not at `ember.elf` itself or a game. If you leave every line commented out, the launcher searches MMCE, USB, exFAT HDD, MX4SIO and memory cards for `EMBER/ember.elf` on its own. APA/PFS hard disks and network shares always need their line.\r\n\r\nThis will be most of the updates for now. I will be putting most of my focus into the main application. In the future I may make a nicer official front end application"
+      }
+    },
