+              "payload": "tree 3d19b6f75d821fcdca9cbb338b5ec73bc06a27f2\nparent e016d934e117a645e476564eddfd7f14f0188e01\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1792337850 -0300\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1792337850 -0300\n\nPADEMU multitap: slot A without an emulated pad uses the real DS2 of the port; each slot keeps its own choice\n\nThe multitap of the chosen port is emulated and used to send everything on that port to the emulator, so the real DS2 of\nthe port stopped working as soon as the multitap option was on.\n\n- pademu: when the emulated multitap has slot A selected and slot A is not emulated, the transfer is left to the hardware\n  (the real pad plugged into the port). Slots B..D are unchanged (no real pad can be there without a real multitap).\n- menu: the emulate checkbox can be changed for every slot in multitap mode; the default 'slots B..D emulated' is applied\n  only when the multitap is switched on (it was forced again on every change and when the dialog opened, so the choice\n  of a slot could not be saved).\n\nNot tested on hardware (no physical multitap available).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GpaNL1s5DWn4V7oBwiutz7\n",
