+            "message": "PADEMU multitap: route each slot / port on its own, also for two-port polls\n\nThe SIO2 hook only handled single-port transfers when the multitap was emulated.\nWhen the game polls port 1 and port 2 in one transfer, the old code ignored the\nselected slot and, with the multitap on port 2, switched off the wrong command\n(the real DS2 of port 1 stopped working).\n\n- pademu_route.h: pure routing rules (real DS2 or emulated pad index) per port,\n  tested on a PC by tools/test_pademu_route.c (555 checks, same result as before\n  for every setup without the multitap)\n- slot A not emulated = the real DS2 of the port; slots B-D always wireless\n- game without multitap support: the multitap port is a plain pad (slot A), the\n  other port stays with the real DS2\n- debug builds log the routing decisions (PADEMU_DEBUG, needs the stdio import)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011XcG3SCVhx3cHqAg5NVAQG",
+            "tree": {
