+              "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MiguelQueiroz010/OPL-DS4RTBT/git/trees/6cbd6389a9351d42957b1c2847a56fcb23298d7c"
+            },
+            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MiguelQueiroz010/OPL-DS4RTBT/git/commits/d8294a02df7d6fe016a4383708cd0a227cef8e52",
+            "comment_count": 0,
+            "verification": {
+              "verified": false,
+              "reason": "no_user",
+              "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA/N0UuB\no407EwjvRs+g3KF8VzjmHFPa7B1VIP6a0Ril2BQj/eE4bdf8LObnEaIZERiqj69upj3n5JvVWVtv\nLgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
+              "payload": "tree 6cbd6389a9351d42957b1c2847a56fcb23298d7c\nparent 9a6c716fb8a67b5493408466e3359e10b9ccf07e\nauthor Miguel Queiroz <bitdrive1raiden@gmail.com> 1792339986 -0300\ncommitter Miguel Queiroz <bitdrive1raiden@gmail.com> 1792339986 -0300\n\nPADEMU multitap: route each slot / port on its own, also for two-port polls\n\nThe SIO2 hook only handled single-port transfers when the multitap was emulated.\nWhen the game polls port 1 and port 2 in one transfer, the old code ignored the\nselected slot and, with the multitap on port 2, switched off the wrong command\n(the real DS2 of port 1 stopped working).\n\n- pademu_route.h: pure routing rules (real DS2 or emulated pad index) per port,\n  tested on a PC by tools/test_pademu_route.c (555 checks, same result as before\n  for every setup without the multitap)\n- slot A not emulated = the real DS2 of the port; slots B-D always wireless\n- game without multitap support: the multitap port is a plain pad (slot A), the\n  other port stays with the real DS2\n- debug builds log the routing decisions (PADEMU_DEBUG, needs the stdio import)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011XcG3SCVhx3cHqAg5NVAQG\n",
