+            },
+            "message": "PADEMU menu: one control per row, new Bluetooth Pads screen\n\nThe Pad Emulator Settings screen put two 50%-wide labels and two controls\non the same row, so the second pair was pushed off screen and overlapped\nthe first (Pad Emulator Mode, Multitap Port, slot Vibration were lost).\n\n- Pad Emulator Settings: one control per row. Each port / multitap slot\n  is a single choice: Off / On / On + Vibration (same settings bits).\n- New Bluetooth Pads screen: adapter MAC, connected pads with type and\n  battery and a Disconnect button each, Search / Pair new pad, DS3 pairing\n  by USB cable (only shown with a DS3 plugged in), fake DS3 workaround and\n  adapter information.\n- Search screen: the adapter/driver debug lines only appear on errors; the\n  pairing message says to press PS to connect.\n- ds34bt: new DS34BT_DISCONNECT RPC (ds34bt_disconnect) that uses the\n  existing DISCONNECT_REQUEST flag of the pad.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxjAGV1NNpMi44hNP3EJTh",
