+            "message": "pademu: start the pad driver early and send the real pad of a mixed poll alone\n\n- The pad driver (Bluetooth adapter / USB pads) now starts on the first pad or\n  multitap command as soon as any pad is enabled, not only when a command\n  reaches an emulated pad. With the multitap emulated and slot A real, the\n  wireless pads had nothing to connect to.\n- 2 port poll with one real and one emulated pad: the real command is sent to\n  the console's SIO2 as a transfer of its own (same buffers, queue holding only\n  that command) instead of running the whole transfer with the emulated\n  command's device byte zeroed, which addressed a device that is not there and\n  could leave padman waiting (\"DMA Busy\").\n- The second command of a 2 port poll is located from the command lengths in\n  regdata (exact); the old byte scan stays as the fallback.\n- tools/test_pademu_split.c: host test of the layout and split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxjAGV1NNpMi44hNP3EJTh",
