+    "release": {
+      "tag": "rc4.5-big-update",
+      "published": "2026-08-31T16:21:20Z",
+      "url": "https://github.com/sobecapaklebs-dev/project-titan-magenta-edition/releases/tag/rc4.5-big-update",
+      "body": "# Project Titan Magenta Edition — BIG UPDATE\r\n\r\nThis release is one of the largest revisions of Project Titan Magenta Edition so far.\r\n\r\nThe **BIG UPDATE** brings a new round of system-level improvements focused on networking, game execution, stability, usability and the native Titan environment.\r\n\r\n> **Project Titan is not just a launcher.**\r\n> It is a PlayStation 2 operating-system project and native application platform with its own boot chain, runtime services, scheduling, package infrastructure, system APIs and integrated game backends.\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n### Cheats & Graphics Enhancements\r\n\r\nProject Titan now includes integrated per-game patch support for both **Titan Neutrino** and **Titan UL**.\r\n\r\nGames can now expose dedicated:\r\n\r\n- **Cheats**\r\n- **Graphics Enhancements**\r\n\r\nmenus directly from the Titan interface.\r\n\r\nThe system supports persistent selections, automatic enhancement presets, experimental patches and safe per-title patch databases.\r\n\r\nWhen graphical enhancements are active, Titan can identify the game as **Titan Enhanced** during launch.\r\n\r\nGameplay cheats are kept separate from visual enhancements, with dedicated handling and a few very Titan-like messages when you decide to make the game a little easier. :)\r\n\r\n### Network improvements\r\n\r\nThis revision contains another significant pass over Titan's network subsystem, including improvements to:\r\n\r\n- network initialization;\r\n- service stability;\r\n- connection handling;\r\n- background network activity;\r\n- resource ownership and cleanup;\r\n- integration with Titan system services.\r\n\r\nThe goal is not only to make networking more reliable, but to continue treating it as a real operating-system service rather than functionality owned by individual applications.\r\n\r\n### Stability improvements\r\n\r\nA large amount of work in this revision happened below the visible interface.\r\n\r\nThe BIG UPDATE includes fixes and hardening across:\r\n\r\n- runtime lifecycle management;\r\n- memory and resource ownership;\r\n- game handoff paths;\r\n- background services;\r\n- storage operations;\r\n- native application execution;\r\n- boot/runtime coordination;\r\n- failure recovery;\r\n- system cleanup between workloads.\r\n\r\nSeveral regressions discovered through real-world testing were also addressed during this development cycle.\r\n\r\n### Native application platform improvements\r\n\r\nProject Titan continues evolving beyond game launching.\r\n\r\nThe system provides its own environment for native Titan applications, including:\r\n\r\n- Titan runtime APIs;\r\n- package installation infrastructure;\r\n- TPKG applications;\r\n- scheduling and lifecycle services;\r\n- shared input, audio, graphics and storage services;\r\n- system notifications;\r\n- networking APIs;\r\n- memory/VRAM management strategies;\r\n- Titan-specific optimization systems for native software.\r\n\r\nGame launching remains an important part of Project Titan, but it is only one subsystem of the larger platform.\r\n\r\n## Game execution\r\n\r\nThe update preserves the established production game backends:\r\n\r\n- **Titan Neutrino**\r\n- **Titan UL**\r\n\r\nwhile adding the new game-patch infrastructure around them without replacing the validated production engine binaries.\r\n\r\nProject Titan now has a cleaner separation between:\r\n\r\n- game execution;\r\n- gameplay cheats;\r\n- graphical enhancements;\r\n- system runtime services.\r\n\r\n## Release packages\r\n\r\nTwo packages are provided.\r\n\r\n### `TITAN_SYSTEM.TINS`\r\n\r\nThe packaged Project Titan system image intended for supported Titan installation/update workflows.\r\n\r\n### Installerless package\r\n\r\nA manual installation package for users who want to deploy the system without using the Titan installer.\r\n\r\nThe installerless layout keeps the normal Titan boot architecture:\r\n\r\n`Memory Card BOOT.ELF → Titan Bootloader → USB kernel.elf → Project Titan`\r\n\r\n## BIG UPDATE\r\n\r\nThis release is called **BIG UPDATE** because it is not centered around one headline feature.\r\n\r\nIt represents another major consolidation of the entire Project Titan platform: networking, game patches, runtime behavior, stability, native applications, system services and many smaller improvements made throughout the project.\r\n\r\nThere is still work ahead — Project Titan remains an ambitious and actively developed system — but this revision moves the project considerably closer to the original goal:\r\n\r\n**turning the PlayStation 2 into a modern, extensible system platform instead of simply giving it another game launcher.**\r\n\r\n**Emotion enhanced.  \r\nFeel the processing.**"
+    }
