+      "body": "OPL Evolution v0.27.0-alpha is the first public prototype release.\n\nThis is an unofficial experimental fork of Open PS2 Loader. Keep Free McBoot,\nwLaunchELF, and a known-good OPL recovery ELF available while testing.\n\nHighlights:\n\n- Standalone Evolution boot flow and dashboard\n- Native PS2 scanning and launching through OPL's loader engine\n- PS1 scanning and launching through an existing POPStarter setup\n- PS2 and PS1 artwork\n- Persistent controller, memory-card, storage, and network widgets\n- Native display and audio controls\n- Save, exit-to-Browser, and power-off system menu\n- Per-game physical, generic, and dedicated VMC assignments\n- 8, 16, 32, and 64 MB VMC creation with progress reporting\n\nKnown limitations:\n\n- Hardware coverage remains limited\n- Network settings are read-only in Evolution\n- Homebrew-library scanning is not complete\n- POPStarter and its required files are not distributed\n- 480p is only suitable for compatible cables, adapters, and displays\n\nThe attached ELF has SHA-256:\n\n`A76B46EA8339E573E46A23DAAD190DE264516D1E9482EF8DA10E04D2BDBBE67B`\n\nPlease include console model, region, storage type/filesystem, video\nconnection, game serial/format, and exact reproduction steps in test reports.\n"
