+      "body": "This is an ALPHA release. It may contain bugs. \r\n\r\nBDM Assault with read-only UDPFS fallback:\r\nif a .VCD file isn't found on the USB drive, POPStarter will attempt to read it from a UDPFS server (udpfsd or udpfs_server.py).\r\n\r\nFiles:\r\n- bdm_udp_fs_assault.irx -> mc?:/POPSTARTER/usbd.irx\r\n- usbd_bd_assault.irx    -> mc?:/POPSTARTER/usbhdfsd.irx\r\n\r\nREADY_TO_USE/POPSTARTER in the archive has both files with the right names.\r\nNo other file is needed: the PS2 uses defaults unless you add the optional IPCONFIG.DAT / UDPFSCONFIG.DAT.\r\n\r\nUsage and what goes where: __bdm_udp_fs_assault/README.MD\r\nNetwork configuration (IPCONFIG.DAT, UDPFSCONFIG.DAT): __bdm_udp_fs_assault/docs/README_CONFIG.txt\r\nThird-party licenses: __bdm_udp_fs_assault/docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\r\n\r\nThis is built specifically for POPStarter, other homebrew are out of scope."
