+  screens and START, as the HDD MANAGER asks. The image (every part; a UL game's ul.cfg made again by the source's
+  own delete), its CFG, its art (COV, COV2, ICO, LAB, LGO, BG, SCR to SCR9), its cheats. Kept unless the user says
+  so: its VMC (saves) and RIPSHOT's full-size shots. A CFG or art another copy of the same game on that drive still
+  uses stays. On the APA HDD the game's partition goes through the driver's own remove (never a __ name, never the
+  partition RIPPS2 runs from or keeps its settings on), and its files in the OPL home after it; the home partition
+  itself is not touched. A PS1 game: its VCD (POPSTARTER) or its game folder (Ember), on a USB, MX4SIO, iLink or
+  exFAT drive. What went is written to mc0:/RIPPS2/REMOVED.TXT.
+
+  The APA check (psx-place's Berion: "APA structure is bond to disk size. By writing disk image, you makes it wrong
+  for your disk if size is different. This leads to APA chain corruption in future."): before a partition goes, the
+  whole chain is read, never written: every header's magic and checksum, each start where the last one's next
+  said, each prev pointing back, every partition a power of two in size and on its own alignment (APA splits free
+  space in halves), none past the disk's end or larger than this disk allows, and the chain closing at __mbr. Any
+  of that wrong and nothing is removed. It runs again after the remove, and the result goes in the receipt.
+*/
